e:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:38:07-07:00","id":847455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=846044#post846044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dont even know where to start kink-shaming this</div> </div> </div> </div> LMFAO. Yeah Amber is so fucked up she's one of my best creations, right up their with my Darkling Hunterheart &quot;Cenobite&quot; and Dearheart/Flamesiren ideas.<br /> <br /> Seriously love this character. And no I don't have a furry fetish, I just love the mix of raw sexuality, animalism, showmenship, and disturbing mix of horror and humour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:19:59-07:00","id":847470,"title":"","content":"Lady Abhilasha is a Fairest Vishkanya (Brewer/Blightbent). An Escort and Assassin, Lady Abhilasha seduces her target then turns either her own bodily fluids into a poison or her targets body fluid into either booze or a poison if the plan is an assassination. When Lady Abhilasha gets really pissed off or is in combat she goes blightbent and turns the moisture in the air around her into alchol (hidden) or poison (lethal damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:16:53-07:00","id":847494,"title":"","content":"Phallic, this is the third female character I've seen you make where a very heavy emphasis was placed on their sexualization. Not sexuality, sexualization. I'm sure many of us are curious to know if you have a changeling character whose only purpose is not to make an appeal as a lustful object, and would love to see a character who is actually, you know, a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:41:42-07:00","id":847511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=847438#post847438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's two of them. Fire having the Crown is by definition Bad News.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the other one? And is their having the Crown a different quality of journalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:24:22-07:00","id":847527,"title":"","content":"If ArcaneArts wouldn't mind me posting a similarly styled character sheet (some things have yet to be filled in proper), I have a character that I've wanted to post since I saw this thread start up. Among the tentative things is the court, since the game I've got planned for is still being planned out, and of the non-Toronto courts thus far Autumn seems like it'd fit Cardiac best. I have other characters, but so far Cardiac is the best laid out.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cardiac Mask</u></b><br /> Wyrd 1 Air-Touched Jeweleyes Elemental (potentially of the Autumn court)<br /> Virtue: Compassion Vice: Violence<br /> Aspirations: Discover his own history, Better function in society, Learn how to drive<br /> Health: 8, Willpower: 6, Clarity: 7<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Mental: Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> Physical: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> Social: Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Mental: Academics 1 (Formal/Essay Writing), Investigation 1, Occult 2<br /> Physical: Athletics 3, Brawl 2 (Counter-attack), Stealth 2, Survival 2, Weaponry 2<br /> Social: Empathy 2, Expression2 (Creative Writing), Intimidation 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Dual Kith<br /> Danger Sense<br /> Indomitable<br /> Patient<br /> Parkour 1<br /> Fighting Style: Armed Defense 1<br /> <br /> <u>Contracts</u><br /> Cloak of Elements (Wind) 1<br /> Pathfinder<br /> Inanimate Communion (Instinctive Knowledge)<br /> Vainglory (Splendor of the Envoy\u2019s Protection)<br /> <br /> <u>Other Traits</u><br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Initiative Mod: 6<br /> Armor: 1/1 when Cloaked<br /> Conditions: Amnesia<br /> Mein: <a href=\"http://s1.tsuki-board.net/pics/figure/large/52751.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Beneath the Mask</a><br /> <br /> <u>Durance</u><br /> <br /> The domain looked like one endless, if empty, city block, pitted with the occasional clearing, park or artificial rivers, and the sky is black...until the Keeper, The Viewer, looks to a certain area. Then the sky is blue but filled with stars, its eyes, hungry to capture the action live. Once lit, Monsters emerge from the shadows and the buildings they have broken into, while Heroes drop down into the streets, and the two fight. Civilians flock out of the buildings to these areas to watch and be taken into the battle.<br /> <br /> Why? Simply because that was the only way to actually get food or water in this realm, aside from eating each other.<br /> <br /> Monsters attack/maim/kill/eat civilians, and while Heroes kill the monsters, they also turn on each other or the civilians as they are given &quot;parts&quot; to play, their memories removed and their personalities given a new mask each time they are to do a &quot;Scene&quot;. The fight lasts until all but one side has died or fled. Then, the eyes descend and fix the damage, reviving the dead and repairing the wounded. However, deceased heroes aren't revived - the wounded are given new powers, because that's what &quot;heroes&quot; do, and coming back from the dead just wasn't &quot;heroic&quot;. Fled heroes are gathered and repaired as well, though perhaps not as well nourished as those who fought and survived.<br /> <br /> Everyone viewed is given sustenance, released and a new part of the city is chosen. Heroes not in the last fight are dispersed here, Monsters who hadn't been involved are drawn in, and new civilians are in willing peril.<br /> <br /> One unfortunate soul happened to wander in through the hedge into the thick of a fight...and he promptly got his face and ribs eaten off. His screams, however, attracted the Eyes of the Viewer, and it proclaimed that, for an amateur, this new person was able to wear his expressions openly, showing and wearing his heart. And so the Viewer &quot;promoted&quot; this poor newcomer to being a Hero. It took his beating heart and made it his face, giving him a new heart in the process, so he would always express himself in the thick of battle, therein known as Heart.<br /> <br /> From that day on, Heart was dropped into different parts of the city where Monsters and civilians flocked, and each time he fought until he won or ran to keep alive. His appearance changed to match the roles the Viewer gave them, as did his fellow Heroes, but his motif remained the same. One day, Heart was doing his duty (as all heroes did) by transcribing what the scene was like from his perspective for the Viewer. However, Heart forgot what hero did which and, remembering that they were with him last scene, looked back at what he wrote before.<br /> <br /> That was what inspired him to run.<br /> <br /> See, Heart noticed that what he wrote before...didn't make sense with what he was writing now. The scene he just did had him as a valiant hero, taking a claw through his chest to protect a civilian. Yet, the previous had him as a dirty coward, begging the monsters to eat his fellow heroes to spare him. And before that he was a brute, fighting anyone and everyone in front of him. On and on, the personalities changed, and though he remembered these scenes it just made <i>no damned sense</i> for him as he read it.<br /> <br /> And then Heart realized that he didn't have a role dictating him - his face was still a heart, but he was remembering himself...as himself. And nothing about what he was remembering was anything he wanted. He wanted stability, he wanted to have consistency. He wouldn't have that here, he couldn't be himself here even between dictations, and unlike the civilians and Monsters he was unlikely stay alive long enough to figure out more.<br /> <br /> And so he ran, into the night that covered much of the city.<br /> <br /> Of course, leaving wasn't easy. Even when the Viewer wasn't watching, the sky dark, Monsters fought him and civilians flocked to him - he was a Hero, and if he was there certainly the Viewer was to come. He ran to the edge of the city and, even then had to scale the buildings to make it over that edge.<br /> <br /> But he made it to the Hedge. As he scrambled through thorns, darkness and maddening views, the idea of stability drew him out and away. When he got out, nameless and without a home, he was as lost as he was in the Viewer's domain. His lack of memory meant that he couldn't recognise his childhood home for what it was, and the face he saw in the windows that didn't click in his memory.<br /> <br /> He still had his mask, however - the heart on his face. The muscle of his heart. The Cardiac. And he took that as his name - Cardiac Mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-15-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:44:44-07:00","id":847534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=847511#post847511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the other one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is their having the Crown a different quality of journalism? </div> </div> </div>It's a little hard to pin down, but by sheer narrative inclination they tend to have a lot of puff pieces in circulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T05:34:57-07:00","id":847632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=847494#post847494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phallic, this is the third female character I've seen you make where a very heavy emphasis was placed on their sexualization. Not sexuality, sexualization. I'm sure many of us are curious to know if you have a changeling character whose only purpose is not to make an appeal as a lustful object, and would love to see a character who is actually, you know, a character.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can branch out. <br /> <br /> Melissa St. Murray<br /> <br /> Seeming: Darkling Kith: Sandharrow<br /> <br /> Melissa was an Oilsands truck Drive in Alberta as a mortal, which is what attracted her Keeper to her.<br /> <br /> During her durance Melissa was shoved into the ground where Arcadian Oilsands seeped into her whole body, binding to every cell. <br /> <br /> She was then dug up and refined into oil then burned to power the factories of Arcadia, and then as smog, fell as black rain, only to combined with sand and dirt to reform into Oilsands again. <br /> <br /> One day she noticed the Changeling digging her out of the ground was exhausted and told him if he spared her this one time, she'd take over his job for the day, allowing him to go into town to have some fun.<br /> <br /> Melissa was an experienced at driving the huge Oilsands trucks and drove right out of Arcadia, plowing her way through the hedge and out into the mortal world.<br /> <br /> The Truck is now a \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 token. <br /> <br /> Melissa joined an enviromentalism group dedicated to stopping the Oilsands, not out of concern for the enviroment, but in the hopes that people stop digging up the Oilsands, maybe she'll be able to stop having horrible dreams about her time AS Oilsands in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Melissa's Keeper is a real bastard. Sometimes he send her dreams about the punishment he inflicted on the poor Truck driver she'd conned into giving up his Truck.<br /> <br /> His punishment makes her ordeal seem pleasant in compareson and Melissa weeps for days after every time her Keeper sends her these dreams (about once a month on the anniversary of her escape).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:26:26-07:00","id":848144,"title":"","content":"This one is more an experiment into whether or not the theme works within the limits of transformation, valid elements for contracts, and the incorporation of a specific horror theme in a game which may or may not fit it.<br /> <br /> Name: Norm<br /> <br /> Concept: Lovecraftian Horror<br /> <br /> Kith: Brollachan/Moonborn<br /> <br /> Seeming: Elemental<br /> <br /> Contracts: Phantom Glory (Element: Slime)<br /> <br /> Merits: Dual Kith 3, Potent Kith 5, Professional Training (Occultist) 2<br /> <br /> Description: Skin near translucent, its hue is that of the blood moon, seeming ever shrouded in shadow. His arms bear multiple thin, boneless limbs much like the arms of an octopus, each extending from just above the forearm, and allowing him to better grapple his prey. His body is tall and slender, moving in an almost alien fashion, like a mere vessel for destruction which no mere man could bring about with their body alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","user":"RichE","date":". 03-16-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:37:56-07:00","id":848266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=848144#post848144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is more an experiment into whether or not the theme works within the limits of transformation, valid elements for contracts, and the incorporation of a specific horror theme in a game which may or may not fit it.<br /> <br /> Name: Norm<br /> <br /> Concept: Lovecraftian Horror<br /> <br /> Kith: Brollachan/Moonborn<br /> <br /> Seeming: Elemental<br /> <br /> Contracts: Phantom Glory (Element: Slime)<br /> <br /> Merits: Dual Kith 3, Potent Kith 5, Professional Training (Occultist) 2<br /> <br /> Description: Skin the near translucent, its hue is that of the blood moon, seeming ever shrouded in shadow. His arms bear multiple thin, boneless limbs much like the arms of an octopus, each extending from just above the forearm, and allowing him to better grapple his prey. His body is tall and slender, moving in an almost alien fashion, like a mere vessel for destruction which no mere man could bring about with their body alone.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love it!!!<br /> <br /> But the name Norm makes me think of Cheers. Arcadia where everybody knows you name and all the True Fae are glad came.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 03-16-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:59:51-07:00","id":848761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=845944#post845944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this character actually have vestigial heads where her boobs used to be or am I misreading this? And if it's the former, what the hell kind of fetishes do you have?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Don't worry, I'm sure Beast will have even crazier ideas eventually. These are role players, we're talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> DeeDee<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Hyperactive Child<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Gremlin<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Fairest<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> To normal people, she appears to be a cute young girl between the ages of 7 and 9 years old with long blond hair and bright green eyes. But to those who can see through her mask, she also possesses a small pair of devil horns and a prehensile tail with an arrow shaped tip. She is fond of wearing pink clothing often decorated with frilly patterns or cute imagery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Durance:</b> In the world of Changelings, DeeDee has accomplished something thought impossible. She didn't just influence her Seeming, but she influenced her Kith as well! DeeDee was taken because her Keeper had a simple wish, she wanted a child of her own. One that she could raise and love just like the human mothers do. Unfortunately for the poor Keeper, she was not prepared for the rambunctious behavior of human children whisked away to a world of magic and dreams. It took all of two minutes after DeeDee was abducted before the girl was bouncing off the walls fascinated by everything around her. In her eagerness to find out how things worked, she ended up breaking the Keeper's possessions more times than she can remember.<br /> <br /> But her Keeper would not physically punish her, no! Mothers were supposed to love their children, not whip them into submission. And so instead she tried to give her a time out and lock DeeDee in her room. That was when DeeDee picked the locks with an untwisted coat hanger from the wardrobe and managed to escape!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-19-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:57:11-07:00","id":849822,"title":"","content":"Mr. Ghast<br /> <br /> Concept: Reformed Boo<br /> <br /> Kith: Gravewight<br /> <br /> Seeming: Elemental<br /> <br /> If he's being honest, Ghast quite likes his new name, and prefers it over his old one (though he still keeps it around for good measure, wearing it like a protective amulet against the Big Nasties out there in the modern bureaucratic world). He was taken by the lord of a decrepit manor in the middle of a misty wood, a Keeper who was fascinated by the concept of ghosts, specifically, ghosts as ahistorical, mischievous spirits. Prankster wights. Fun-loving haunters. Granted, in Faerie, practical jokes can be incredibly lethal, and the falling chandeliers, bloodthirsty pianos, and artfully-weakened floorboards over spike pits were constant dangers to visitors.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ghast was turned into a ghost. He doesn't think he was killed, per se; the Gentry merely reshaped his body into a more ethereal form. Some days, he was possessing an armchair to wrap itself around an unwary guest. Other times he appeared in the reflection of a cracked mirror, blood streaming from his eyeless sockets. The Ghost Lord loved nothing more than to lure travelers to the manor and see how long they would last in the spook house. Those unfortunates were often drafted as new recruits in the Ghost Lord's domain.<br /> <br /> There was always a way out, though, some trick to solving the house's puzzles and traps and getting out alive on the other side. Maybe the Ghost Lord had a sense of fairness, or maybe it was a Catch in the Contracts that held his domain together. Whatever the case, there was always a way for the clever and resourceful to get out alive. Ghast became obsessed with one such hopeful, a changeling sent on as a diplomatic envoy be a foreign Keeper. He followed her around the manor, unseen, manipulating events just so, to give her a fighting chance of surviving. She came out the other side, frightened, shaken, a long cut down her left arm, but unmangled, still alive and with all her internal organs.<br /> <br /> Infused with essence of the ghost house, and with a sudden burst of memory of being something other than a spectre, Mr. Ghast found himself outside, in the Hedge. From there, he beat a path back home to Earth and too-solid flesh.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, Ghast is trying to figure himself out. He still enjoys scaring people, to an extent, but malevolent deception is a Clarity Breaking Point for him. Hurting others through misdirection reminds him of his time in the ghost house, and how nothing could ever truly be what it seemed. But on the other hand, it's what he's good at. Perhaps the Scarecrow Ministry will take him, one day, if he proves himself. He's also been learning some things about ghosts--real ghosts, the ones with histories and survivors they left behind. Most are fully uninterested in pranks. This is new to him. Maybe he can provide them with a home, a special haunt of their own, a safe space to gather and remember their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T18:14:32-07:00","id":850350,"title":"","content":"Go the eyes Boo! <br /> <br /> Bonus points for getting the reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T19:00:59-07:00","id":850358,"title":"","content":"Espritdecalmar, I really like Mr. Ghast. He gives me a Jack Skellington and Cartoon!Beetlejuice vibe. Or a Tim Burton-esque vibe in general. I just don't know if Elemental is the right Seeming for him. Since his escape involved helping someone instead of being the carefree troublemaker his Keeper thinks ghosts should be, I believe Mr. Ghast is a Fairest. He even seeks to help real ghosts, who often have dark and traumatic pasts. That's not for everyone, and indeed, most would be too afraid to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-21-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T19:24:03-07:00","id":850367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=850350#post850350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go the eyes Boo!<br /> <br /> Bonus points for getting the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Cover your nose, Boo. We will leave no crevice untouched!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:55:06-07:00","id":850593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=850358#post850358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Espritdecalmar, I really like Mr. Ghast. He gives me a Jack Skellington and Cartoon!Beetlejuice vibe. Or a Tim Burton-esque vibe in general. I just don't know if Elemental is the right Seeming for him. Since his escape involved helping someone instead of being the carefree troublemaker his Keeper thinks ghosts should be, I believe Mr. Ghast is a Fairest. He even seeks to help real ghosts, who often have dark and traumatic pasts. That's not for everyone, and indeed, most would be too afraid too try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. And that's fair. I went with Elemental because I thought the Seeming Curse was particularly fitting for him. But there's definitely a case for Fairest to be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:04:22-07:00","id":850599,"title":"","content":"Yes, Baulder's Gate!!! Butt kicking for Justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:17:43-07:00","id":850605,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Name:</b> BunBun<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Strip Club Owner<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Dancer<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Beast<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Covered in bright pink fur with long, floppy ears and a short, fluffy tail, BunBun resembles an anthropomorphic bunny. His physical build is so girly, he can be mistaken for a transgender at first, but the stern expression on his lapin face makes it clear he is in absolutely no mood for jokes. His mask resembles a young man with the build of an acrobat and with pink dyed hair. He is frequently dressed in black leather / latex outfits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> The subject of a cruel joke by his Keeper, the one known as BunBun was possessed of a violent temperment and controlling attitude. So when he was taken away, his Keeper transformed his body into a harem boy, who's features were cute and effeminate. Being forced to dance for his much stronger master, BunBun's aggressive tendencies only grew until they finally exploded in a violent outburst. During his last performance, he delivered a flying drop kick to his Keeper's groin and proceeded to leap out a window to freedom, crashing through the decorative glass and landing in the real world.<br /> <br /> Despite having a body that many would consider harmless, BunBun is both respected and feared by the rest of the Freehold. Since his escape, he has become the proprietor of a bisexual strip club (Sweet Release) that caters to supernatural clientele. He rules this establishment with an iron fist and cracks down hard on anybody caught disrupting the flow of business in his club. He has sent many trouble makers to the hospital already and is not shy about doing so again. The employees who work for him claim that they are safer with BunBun than they are on the street, but he can be a demanding task master in exchange for the protection he offers.<br /> <br /> BunBun is the leader of his Motley (named after his club) for more than just his leadership skills. The rest of the Motley actually work at Sweet Release, which makes him their boss since he owns the place. Not every worker at the club is a member, but enough of them are that he's able to keep tabs on the club's activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-21-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T08:34:20-07:00","id":851160,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Name:</b> Pasop<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Street Snitch<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Troll + Minstrel<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Darkling<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> In his mien, Pasop exhibits the body of a cartoon meerkat straight out of a Disney production who stands at a scrawny 4'0 tall. His eyes are often scanning the environment as if he's expecting something to jump out at him at any moment. When in his mask, he appears as a dark skinned boy with short black hair. He is fond of wearing baggy pants as he claims they fit better in his mien. He is also known to wear a recon vest over his shirt, which he keeps packed with supplies in case he needs them.<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> It is not uncommon for the True Fae to find pleasure in mortal entertainment, especially when they have no imagination of their own. This was the case with Pasop's former master who had a great love for cartoon animals. More specifically, it enjoyed worlds in which the animals were perfectly sentient, yet still hunted each other for food. After he was taken, Pasop awoke to find he had been dumped in a scenery that looked like it belonged in The Lion King. He also quickly noticed that he was now in the body of a cartoon meerkat and only 12 inches tall!<br /> <br /> During his stay in Arcadia, Pasop had two roles that his Keeper demanded of him. The first role was that he act as sentry for his meerkat colony, warning them of incoming predators so they could take shelter in their underground burrows. The second was that he was expected to be able to participate in spontaneous musical numbers that often came without any provocation or rehearsal. Needless to say, this was a very embarrassing time in his life, but he managed to escape one day when he refused to warn the colony of an attack. Instead, when Pasop detected the predators, he fled to safety while leaving the others behind as a sacrifice to appease the hungry carnivores, eventually finding his way back through the Hedge and into the world of humanity once more.<br /> <br /> Pasop's name means &quot;Lookout&quot; in Afrikaans, which is appropriate given his role there. Since his escape, he has resumed this service by prowling the streets of the Freehold in search of dangerous predators (like the Huntsmen) and informing nearby security of encroaching threats. He is also constantly bragging about his new mix tape and encouraging people to listen to it!<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Hex<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Witchtooth<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Beast<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Her mien appears almost human with the exception of having the eyes, tail and ears of a black cat. Both in her mien and mask, she wears Gothic attire consisting of a fishnet outfit worn underneath a black tank top and skirt. She also wears buckle strapped boots that go up to her thighs, and black gloves that extend to her elbows. Her hair is long and black, and she wears dark eyeliner to give her eyes a more feline style. Her physical appearance suggests she is 16 years of age.<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Hex's Keeper found her during her goth phase that was common among angsty teenage girls. Normally the curses she tried to place on people were just a way to vent her frustration and get on with it. She couldn't have known that last spell would actually get the attention of an otherworldly being! Intrigued by her performance, the Fae promised to satisfy her grudge while teaching her about real magic. Hex agreed, but didn't realize the cost of her bargain until too late.<br /> <br /> True to its word, her Keeper took her back home and began to instruct her in the use of magic, but the spells she had her instructed in were of the black arts. Among some of the more shocking rituals she took part in included stealing the life force of children, blood sacrifices, and whoring her body out to demons! This wasn't the kind of witchcraft that Wiccans believed in, this was the witchraft that normal people believed in. She had to escape, and after months of practice, she developed the spell that would enable her to do so.<br /> <br /> Hex discovered a spell that would enable her to change her form, presumably to avoid her Keeper's notice while she fled to the human world. She chose the form of a black cat (she still doesn't know why) and slunk off into the night while her Keeper was preparing another ritual. Upon her return to the human world, Hex attempted to undo the spell but found it was significantly harder than before. She ended up fainting from exhaustion only to awaken later in a Freehold infirmary. The stress of the miscast spell caused her to suffer amnesia, forgetting her real name. She also forgot most of the magic she learned with her Keeper, including how to fully regain her human form, leaving her as a partially transformed hybrid. Yet despite losing most of her accumulated knowledge, she retains a natural talent for the occult and with the help of the Freehold has begun to relearn what she lost.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:20:40-07:00","id":852808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=850605#post850605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Name:</b> BunBun<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Strip Club Owner<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Dancer<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Beast<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Covered in bright pink fur with long, floppy ears and a short, fluffy tail, BunBun resembles an anthropomorphic bunny. His physical build is so girly, he can be mistaken for a transgender at first, but the stern expression on his lapin face makes it clear he is in absolutely no mood for jokes. His mask resembles a young man with the build of an acrobat and with pink dyed hair. He is frequently dressed in black leather / latex outfits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> The subject of a cruel joke by his Keeper, the one known as BunBun was possessed of a violent temperment and controlling attitude. So when he was taken away, his Keeper transformed his body into a harem boy, who's features were cute and effeminate. Being forced to dance for his much stronger master, BunBun's aggressive tendencies only grew until they finally exploded in a violent outburst. During his last performance, he delivered a flying drop kick to his Keeper's groin and proceeded to leap out a window to freedom, crashing through the decorative glass and landing in the real world.<br /> <br /> Despite having a body that many would consider harmless, BunBun is both respected and feared by the rest of the Freehold. Since his escape, he has become the proprietor of a bisexual strip club (Sweet Release) that caters to supernatural clientele. He rules this establishment with an iron fist and cracks down hard on anybody caught disrupting the flow of business in his club. He has sent many trouble makers to the hospital already and is not shy about doing so again. The employees who work for him claim that they are safer with BunBun than they are on the street, but he can be a demanding task master in exchange for the protection he offers.<br /> <br /> BunBun is the leader of his Motley (named after his club) for more than just his leadership skills. The rest of the Motley actually work at Sweet Release, which makes him their boss since he owns the place. Not every worker at the club is a member, but enough of them are that he's able to keep tabs on the club's activities.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really like this one. I had a good chuckle, but I was also intrigued. He seems like he could an excellent spy and information broker, what with his harmless/beautiful looks. He could develop Whisperwisp as a second Kith. He also sounds like a good candidate for mind-control Contracts. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:35:32-07:00","id":852811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=852808#post852808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really like this one. I had a good chuckle, but I was also intrigued. He seems like he could an excellent spy and information broker, what with his harmless/beautiful looks. He could develop Whisperwisp as a second Kith. He also sounds like a good candidate for mind-control Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> BunBun is actually a recycled character from a previous RP series I took part in. Though he's been edited to fit the Changeling universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin