Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T23:15:34-07:00","id":853355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=853343#post853343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey guys if i share an npc writeup from the chicago game will you stop talking about sexhouses</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No promises. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T23:35:46-07:00","id":853358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=853355#post853355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No promises.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Changeling thread? You ought to know better.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, guys, come on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T23:51:21-07:00","id":853361,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Name:</b> Mr. Bushido<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Repentant Soldier<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Razorhand<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Fairest<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Mr. Bushido appears to be of Japanese ethnicity with dark black hair that he wears in a top knot and sports a thin goatee as facial hair. He dresses in traditional Japanese robes and always carries a sword on his person. When in his Mask, the sword is either concealed from public notice or disguised as another instrument, and although his features are still Japanese, they are less traditional style and more appropriate to the modern time period.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Having abandoned his real name, the one known as Mr. Bushido has a bloody history that he is not comfortable to speak of even among friends. One spring morning while taking a walk through the forest, he was snatched by a True Fae and dragged off to their oriental realm. There he was rigorously instructed in the way of swordsmanship and loyalty, becoming the iconic archetype of a samurai. To serve his Keeper, he was presented with a cursed sword. The moment Mr. Bushido wrapped his fingers around it, he was unable to break physical contact with the weapon ever again. It was bound to him now, as much a part of his body as his arm or leg!<br /> <br /> For many years (in Fae terms), Mr. Bushido defended his Keeper's realm from invaders while simultaneously crushing the peasants that tried to rebel against his tyrannical rule. But then the unthinkable happened; he failed to defeat his enemy. By the code of the samurai, he should have taken his own life on the spot when his opponent chose to spare him, but something awoke inside him and he began to remember. This was not his home, this was not even his real time period, someone or something had dragged him here by force, brainwashed him to be the perfect warrior. Reeling from the shock of his memories, he chose to join the rebels and help them return to freedom by cutting down the soldiers he once served beside!<br /> <br /> Since his escape, Mr. Bushido seeks to make amends for the blood he shed serving his Keeper. No longer seeing the honor in slaying an enemy, he kills only when it is necessary instead of when his pride compels him to do so. Even then, he does so with a heavy heart, as it adds more guilt that he must atone for before he can rest peacefully.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T05:24:39-07:00","id":853425,"title":"","content":"Satchel is right. The joke has run its course. Sorry if I contributed to the derailing.<br /> <br /> By the way, I really like Mr. Bushido. I think it would be cool if he really was taken from feudal Japan, and the Arcadian flow of time took him to Japan in the 21st century. The &quot;fish out of temporal water&quot; backstory shared by some changelings is a good source of drama that is a bit overlooked. <br /> <br /> Nyrufa, speaking of being lost in time, how would you do a changeling similar to Fry from Futurama? Not the actual Fry, mind you, but something within the same ballpark.<br /> <br /> As an aside, if you combined Mr. Bushido with that Anakim Ravager who looks like a heavy metal black knight from the Beast Ideas thread, you'd get pretty close to my favorite PC.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering what combination of Kith and Seeming is the best for an &quot;ultimate thief&quot; kind of character. I was thinking of something like Sly Cooper and Sam Fisher, who fancies himself a gentleman and Robin Hood-esque figure, but falls short of the ideal. Probably a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:58:27-07:00","id":853474,"title":"","content":"For making a Fry character, I think most of the main cast would fit well as Changelings in a Motley.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amy's a Fairest<br /> <br /> Lila's an Ogre<br /> <br /> Bender's a Darkling<br /> <br /> Zoidberg's a Beast<br /> <br /> Fry's <i>possibly</i> a Grimm<br /> <br /> The rest are undecided.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, for the Sly Cooper style character, I would suggest blending him with a Coyote, given their reputation as tricksters. Especially since he steals exclusively from his fellow criminals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other Kiths that might work as a combination include Farwalker (slipping past all that security), Larcenist (obviously), Runnerswift (he's pretty agile), Skitterskulk (platforming skills), Slewfoot (for completionist bonus).<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, I would say that Larcenist + Slewfoot would be the best combination if you want to fit the style of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for his Seeming, I'm going to say he's a <b>Fairest</b>. He doesn't really fit the role of a Beast because the people in his world are civilized animals. But as a character, he's the leader of a group of thieves, his family's skills are legendary, he managed to seduce the very detective assigned to arrest him <i>multiple times</i>, and he makes other criminals look like fools just for the thrill of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:19:24-07:00","id":854289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=853326#post853326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aHAPcTx_FNc\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Speaking of sex and D&amp;D...</b></a> (NSFW, obviously)<br /> Fall-From-Grace, a succubus from Planescape: Torment who runs a brothel where you slake <i>intellectual </i>lusts.</div> </div> </div> </div> I bet you 20 bucks that if one opened up a place like that that for real they'd do suprisingly well.<br /> <br /> Okay Fall-From-Grace as a Changeling.<br /> <br /> Seeming: Darkling Kith: Dearest/Fireheart Court: Brass<br /> <br /> Contracts: Shared Burden \u2022\u2022\u2022, Vainglory \u2022\u2022","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:20:10-07:00","id":854563,"title":"","content":"<b>Lazlo Blue-Blood</b>, Displaced Patrician<br /> <b>Darkling Earthbones</b> of the <b>Wind Court</b><br /> <b>Mask/Mien:</b> Guru/Martyr<br /> <br /> <u><b>Description</b></u><br /> It\u2019s not easy to look Lazlo in the eye. Even those who only see the Mask can tell two things from such brief contact - he is very old and very guilty. His eyes stare out from above hollow cheeks, his skin is pale verging on bloodless, and his comportment is seldom without a nervous tic.<br /> <br /> His fae mien is even more unsettling, from his sunken eye sockets to the facial scar that weeps a turquoise blue ichor to the twitching spider legs that sometimes stick out from the cracks in his gray marble flesh - as a changeling, Lazlo looks like a hideously warped statue carved from the earthen prison of something terrible.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> Lazlo inherited a philanthropic legacy rooted in one of the success stories of the American Dream. He used to be as near as one gets to modern nobility in both name and deed, fighting the political corruption that plagued his city\u2019s very reputation tooth and nail at personal expense.<br /> <br /> Lazlo was, in short, a veritable pillar of the community. The Stranger Cevexh, in common fae fashion, took this rather more literally than most when she had him hauled off to Arcadia. She made a stone column of his fortitude, to raise her arena above the thorns and briars that crawled across her domain, and left him below to support her decadence.<br /> <br /> He stayed like this for a time, listening to the noise of gladiator fights by day and warding off creeping vines and questing roots by night, until one evening Cevexh\u2019s best-loved prizefighter was given a leave of absence. Struck by the injustice of this favoritism, the pillar that was Lazlo set forth a litany of the indignities he had been subjected to while trapped away from his home.<br /> <br /> The declamation stretched for seeming hours and was tinged with such poison that the Hedge-plants withered around him, and when he finally came to a stop he was shocked to find that the rose-child was still standing before him. Stranger still, through the haze of his shame he realized that the duelist was offering to take him away from the arena if he would only show the boy the world of his birth.<br /> <br /> He accepted, and since leaving Faerie the weight has not lifted from his shoulders.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Personality</u></b><br /> Despite his gloomy outlook, Lazlo has adapted easily to the fae currents of favor and obligation, rapidly trading and networking his way to both a clerical position at City Hall and an administrative office as Treasurer of the Looking-Glass Court. His pride demands that he fall no further, and to that end he has become one of the most well-connected changelings in Chicago.<br /> <br /> There are several reasons Lazlo has thrown himself so entirely into his role in the freehold. Like many of the Lost, he left a family behind when his Keeper pulled him into her tale, and he does not trust in his ability to step into his old life when his political activity already put significant distance between him and his children.<br /> <br /> Instead, he has made a minor habit of adopting newly escaped changelings as prot\u00e9g\u00e9s, pushing them to strive for whatever pursuits mesh with his own unfulfilled dreams. He commiserates with the bitter Arcadian intern at Newcomb and Razor over the frustrations of fetch-trickery, tutors the Flowering ex-gladiator in the subtleties of the Blue Court\u2019s relation to the Red, and otherwise fans those sparks of similitude he comes across as he quietly worries at the cracks in his flagging ego","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:59:51-07:00","id":854709,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (The) Ziband</span><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Aspires to Godhood</span><br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Witchtooth + Coyote</span><br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Fairest</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> An anthropomorphic coyote with sandy colored fur and dressed in human clothing. He is fond of the colors yellow, purple, and green, often incorporating these colors into his outfit in some way. His mask appears to be an attractive Caucasian man with sandy brown hair that sticks out in short, spiky tufts about his head. He is frequently seen wearing a smirk that lays somewhere between proud satisfaction and the edge of madness.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details: </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Before he was taken, The Ziband was a nihilist who found the human world to be dull, boring and pointless. Everything was repetitive where nothing out of the ordinary happened anymore. Perhaps it was this melancholy disposition that drew the Fae to him, but one day he was approached by his Keeper who promised to show him a world of magic and splendor. All it would cost him is to abandon the only world he had ever known and come live with a nigh omnipotent, alien being from another dimension!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">During his stay, his Keeper showed him secrets, <i>so very many secrets</i>, and Ziband soaked them up like a sponge. But it was never enough; no matter how much he learned about Arcadia, he was incapable of figuring out most of it on his own. His Keeper had to explain things to him as if he were an idiot child unaware of what he was doing. His human mind simply could not grasp the nature of a realm forged out of dreams and metaphor, where logic and common sense did not apply to the forces of nature. Eventually, Ziband could no longer stand his perpetual ignorance and fled back to the human world vowing he would return when he was more properly equipped to handle Arcadia's magical nature.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Since his &quot;escape&quot; from Arcadia, Ziband has devoted his efforts towards increasing his power first and foremost. He is a resident of the Freehold, but has not pledged himself to any Court, instead remaining an independent agent. As a Witchtooth, he is constantly researching occult knowledge and hoarding magical artifacts. While as a Coyote, he is fiendishly manipulating everybody who interacts with him, be they friends or enemies. He is still juggling with the idea of what he should do with his closest allies. So far, he's likes the idea of becoming their new Keeper once he feels ready to return to the world of the Fae.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ziband's long term goal is to return to Arcadia not as a slave, but as a noble. He seeks to gentrify himself and become one with the True Fae, believing that in doing so, he will obtain godly power and be able to warp reality to his will. Naturally, nobody in the Freehold knows about this plan of his, not even those who he calls <i>friends.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Note: </b>Ziband has a personality quirk of speaking about himself in the third person, often adding &quot;the&quot; at the beginning of his name. He also tends to have very high opinions of himself, not dissimilar from a celebrity diva that mingles with common folk. To some, this quirk is entertaining (in small doses), while to others, it can grow tiresome and annoying.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:01:24-07:00","id":855425,"title":"","content":"I admit I have not stayed quite up to date of the Changeling front, but I like the ideas people are sharing. May have to throw something of my own together here soon...<br /> <br /> Never actually managed to participate in a 1e game, and the the only Changeling character I ever worked on stats for was a Coyote/Windwing Sphinx. (Didn't have the book for the Riddleseeker kith, so I made do with what I had.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 03-29-2016, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:25:15-07:00","id":855432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=855425#post855425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I have not stayed quite up to date of the Changeling front, but I like the ideas people are sharing. May have to throw something of my own together here soon...<br /> <br /> Never actually managed to participate in a 1e game, and the the only Changeling character I ever worked on stats for was a Coyote/Windwing Sphinx. (Didn't have the book for the Riddleseeker kith, so I made do with what I had.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's okay, I've got 1E core book, vamp, and werewolf and never actually played them, either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:48:49-07:00","id":855488,"title":"","content":"I've got a huge pile of unused/not-completely-read books. Been trying to do something about that recently, though. Getting started with a mortal, hoping to try a wolf or 'ling next. Mage looks fun, but it's rules heavy, so very rules heavy.<br /> <br /> As for that Sphinx, he was the kind of person who'd give great advice, insightful in what people wanted and needed, he just expressed it by baiting and antagonizing people until he had them pointed in the right direction. Lots of leading questions and teasing one-off comments. Fidgety as hell too.<br /> <br /> His durance saw him as one of the various monsters tasked with guarding a castle from a group of invaders, led by his keeper in the form of a shining knight, who would defeat them all time and time again. After the first several cycles of getting himself wounded or killed trying to fight them off, and he learned exactly what the punishment for not trying was, he settled into an 'Answer me these questions three' routine that the keeper found entertain enough to play along with, eventually earning him the form in which he'd escape.<br /> <br /> That escape came when, after an uncountable number of repetitions on the same scenario, he challenged the knights, as he always would, lost as he had done many times before, and threw himself off the tower, which was new, dramatic sure, but more importantly, it left the knights declaring loudly that they had 'vanquished the monster', and continuing on their way.<br /> <br /> They had apparently forgotten he had perfectly good wings at the time. He'd fly far, far away, over the moats, the outer walls, and the invading army. He'd fly until the distant plains gave way to thorns that tore his wings apart, dragged him down to the ground, and then he'd run, and run, and run, and never look back. Until he found himself in the outside world.<br /> <br /> That would make him a... Grimm in 2e? Or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 03-30-2016, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:26:31-07:00","id":855499,"title":"","content":"Personally, I couldn't wrap my head around Wolf, it seemed way too complicated for me. But then again, I was already familiar with Vampire thanks to Masquerade Bloodlines while having next to no information about Werewolf. So going in, it was like having one game I already knew the general theme of, and another game I had to learn from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <br /> In hindsight, I wish I had bought Changeling instead of Wolf, because it seems like an awesome setting / concept!<br /> <br /> At the moment, Changeling is probably my favorite nWoD setting, and I haven't even read the book. Just going by what I've been told about it is enough to get me hyped!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> But yeah, that does sound like it would fit with the Grimm type character. From what we've been told, Grimms are Changelings who took control of the story they were forced to participate in, writing a new ending for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-30-2016, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:40:46-07:00","id":922855,"title":"","content":"Second Chicago NPC writeup.<br /> <br /> <b>Terri Caulfield</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, Reclusive Surveyor</span></span><br /> <b>Beast Levinquick</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> of the </span></span><b>Fire Court</b><br /> <b>Mask/Mien:</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Survivor/Monster</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Description</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The rare occasions that Terri\u2019s human face can be seen tend to take their toll on her presentation; a scattering of premature grey hairs break up her ragged black bob-cut, her eyes are sunken and wide, and what can be seen of her teeth are pitted and chipped within bloody gums. A tattered red shawl hangs on her slight frame over one of various outfits picked from a handful of cheap dress shirts and pairs of worn-down denim pants. Terri is usually barefoot, which makes it hard not to notice she\u2019s missing a toe on either foot.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She\u2019s more in her element in the Hedge, where her mien need not go through such an awkward translation. Caulfield looks mouselike beneath the Mask, her glass teeth and glass eyes glinting in the patchy neon light that lines her Hedgespun cloak of bloody sawgrass. Despite being smaller than some children she still cuts an intimidating figure \u2014 her black pelt fades into the background as the jagged white markings upon it stretch off her ears and tail into the sky. She is seldom empty-handed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Background</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If she is honest \u2014 and she usually is \u2014 Terri thinks the Storm-Serpent Marquess might have taken her out of a misplaced sense of pity. The Levinquick recalls catching glimpses of the Fae during her strict apprenticeship as an electrician in attics and basements. The Huntsman sent to pick her up orchestrated the power outage that was her first job as a journeyman, and the older residents of that building still whisper stories of the freak storm that brought her there and grumble over the fallout from the fumbling repairs her fetch left it with.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Terri lived for a time on the stormy scrubland of her Keeper\u2019s vast estate, herded with her fellow captives from outpost to fencepost to lonely outpost by ill winds and low-hanging thunderstorms. Many of the changelings in her company were broken by the years of highly regimented drills and harrowing near-miss evacuations, eventually fleeing to the plains to meet whatever fate the Marquess had in store for deserters; the Beast saw some of their twisted remains on her desperate flight through curtains of thunder the night she stole her handler\u2019s key, scattered her comrades, and made her escape in the ensuing chaos to the hills above the advancing thunderheads.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Caulfield returned to Earth in the same attic the scarecrow of rat skulls and copper wire was left, during the last of many blackouts enabled by the imposter\u2019s substandard fix. It would prove a sign of things to come that she was discovered by one of the rare few mortals who could see through the Mask in the middle of an attempt to sort the matter out; the ensuing panic only ended when she joined the Court of Fire some hours later. After a few months of trying and failing to adjust to active life in the freehold, she largely retreated from society until the early twenty-tens. Her renewed involvement with the Underwood began with her </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">formal claim of the role of Surveyor, citing inspiration from the previous appointee\u2019s grandson and one of the many visiting fae that pass through Chicago.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Personality</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Terri has gotten moderately far in life on her ability to divert attention away from herself. Despite her burgeoning reputation as an ill omen among the freehold, the Beast is a natural fit for the post of Surveyor, being well-practiced at cold-reading and keeping a conversation going. She does poorly with direct confrontation, being both noise-averse and a terrible liar, but neither of these qualities interfere much with the aura of panic that pervades the Hedge around her and empowers her bond to the Lantern Court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Despite her forthright nature and the social requirements of her appointed task, Caulfield is functionally a recluse for much of the year; her brief stint as Crown Princess and her key role in maintaining the Bulwark have instilled the reserve Lamplighter with a firm belief that the best thing she can do for Chicago proper is to keep her visits as short as possible.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:52:58-07:00","id":923011,"title":"","content":"So keep in mind I'm fairly new to Changeling and I'm lacking basically everything from 2.0 since I'm having a hard time finding the resources when people point out stuff like Potent Kith mentioned earlier, so this is mostly pure fluff and doesn't have a dot-by-dot breakdown of the sheet or anything since I don't even know where to begin.<br /> <br /> Name: Toski, the Dream Delver<br /> Age: Mask is his 30's of a person with dwarfism, bright red hair and green eyes. Like a knee-to-middlethigh-height Weasley. <br /> Kith: Still working this out, but likely Chiurgeon / Truefriend or some kind of one like a gardener. <br /> Court: Spring<br /> <br /> Toski is a bit of an unusual one. For one, to changelings he looks like a humanoid squirrel, complete with snout, bushy tail, ears, and fur. But that's not all. He wasn't originally human. Technically, he's a hobgoblin, but mechanically built as a changeling, spawned from a rather unlucky squirrel that happened to wander into an open hedge gate under the roots of a large oak in a city park that had been there since its founding and was the main way the local Fae abducted people. You know those little shreds of left-behind soul from a changeling as they're yanked through the thorns? He ended up finding a piece and, being a dumb squirrel, tried gnawing on it thinking it was food. Since the Wyrd has a sick sense of humor, it rather unpleasantly hot-glued that essence of humanity to him with a dose of glamour, giving him fragmented, but usable memories of humanity and twisting him into his current shape. Once he managed to get back out after a few months of wandering, he took up the name Toski, after Ratatoskr, the great messenger squirrel that darted among the branches of the world tree, delivering messages. In his case, the branches are the dreams of others, delivering warnings of incoming attacks, delivering message of new changeling arrivals, and generally being a very valuable informant for the Spring Court by keeping an eye on the local hedge. Takes his payment as bottled, honest laughter (as opposed to forced, fake laughter. The laugh and the joy that comes with it have to be genuine) and distills it into a healing goblin fruit farm for his motley, since as they say laughter is the best medicine. <br /> <br /> No slouch helping out physically, either. That Spring control of plants as well as a few contracts of the Hedge are very useful for, say providing food or growing gnarled roots almost a foot thick as a wall to block pursuers.<br /> <br /> His spring mantle also manifests as a strong, flowery perfume that seems to follow him, and occasionally flowers will bloom from his fur similar to a fashion accessory. Like one might bloom on his upper chest as if he had a lapel pin. Wears a necklace with viking runes as a kind of reminder and affirmation of his Spring Court allegiances. Possibly a token, but no clue on potential effects: <br /> <br /> Barkanan: <span style=\"font-family:Libre Baskerville, serif\"><span style=\"color:#2b2b2b\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">symbolizing fertility, growth, sustenance, and healing. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Libre Baskerville, serif\"><span style=\"color:#2b2b2b\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ingwaz: Fertilization, the start of something new, actualization of potential.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Libre Baskerville, serif\"><span style=\"color:#2b2b2b\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dagaz: Hope, happiness</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Naudhiz: Need, unfulfilled desire</span></span></span><br /> Jera: Harvest / reward<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Libre Baskerville, serif\"><span style=\"color:#2b2b2b\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">and Wunjo: Joy, ecstasy. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T13:08:21-07:00","id":923437,"title":"","content":"Interesting, I concidered the possiblity that someone might want to Cambions, Fetches, heck even rogue Huntsmen, as well as the Changeling and Fae Touched, but not that someone who want to play a verison of a Hedge Beast Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:11:52-07:00","id":923513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=923437#post923437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, I concidered the possiblity that someone might want to Cambions, Fetches, heck even rogue Huntsmen, as well as the Changeling and Fae Touched, but not that someone who want to play a verison of a Hedge Beast Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no rules that forbid it that I'm aware of. Part of the fun of Changeling is to be bizarre, strange, and fantastic just as much as creepy, unsettling, and messed up. It even mentions that hobgoblins come in nearly every shape and form imaginable since they're basically imagination made flesh as if Willy Wonka got ahold of a Disney ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:19:35-07:00","id":977887,"title":"","content":"After reading over the old thread on 2e Wizened, I had the idea of a Brolachan Wizened that, rather than changing his body to be a perfect bringer of fear, changed himself to be a gardener. He was assigned to torment the poor souls that found their way into the Keepers forest, but he took comfort in the forest, tending it and such when he could, making himself more and more into a gardener, until he was able to make his escape thanks to his knowledge of the woods and such.<br /> <br /> He would probably look kind of like a hunched man made entirely of ebony wood, with stark, white eyes. he has claws he uses as gardening shears, that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> I know that sounds kind of like a woodwalker, but the way kith and seeming work now is supposed to provide more options, so I figured I'd go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:45:40-07:00","id":977906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=923513#post923513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no rules that forbid it that I'm aware of. Part of the fun of Changeling is to be bizarre, strange, and fantastic just as much as creepy, unsettling, and messed up. It even mentions that hobgoblins come in nearly every shape and form imaginable since they're basically imagination made flesh as if Willy Wonka got ahold of a Disney ride.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:46:29-07:00","id":977908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=977887#post977887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading over the old thread on 2e Wizened, I had the idea of a Brolachan Wizened that, rather than changing his body to be a perfect bringer of fear, changed himself to be a gardener. He was assigned to torment the poor souls that found their way into the Keepers forest, but he took comfort in the forest, tending it and such when he could, making himself more and more into a gardener, until he was able to make his escape thanks to his knowledge of the woods and such.<br /> <br /> He would probably look kind of like a hunched man made entirely of ebony wood, with stark, white eyes. he has claws he uses as gardening shears, that kind of thing. <br /> <br /> I know that sounds kind of like a woodwalker, but the way kith and seeming work now is supposed to provide more options, so I figured I'd go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could always dual kith, in fact this Characters background sounds perfect for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:43:14-07:00","id":978678,"title":"","content":"This is a idea I was working on for a predessigned character for a one shot of a Changeling game. I ended the character development here, I got inspiration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Isabella<br /> <b>Seeming</b>: Fairest<br /> <b>Kith Idea</b>: The Dark Knight (Female <b>Fairest</b> dual kith <b>Razorhand / Metalflesh</b>). Her razorhand weapon is a sword masked in the form of a sword pendant, and when she invokes her Metalflesh armor, it apears in a suit of dark plate mail.<br /> <b>Concept</b>: former Gentry enforcer, leader of the Dark King's armies<br /> <b>Merits ideas</b>: Fae Mount (Tintaglia), Dual Kith, Potent kith.<br /> <b>Motto</b>: Those who abuse the weak are weak themselves. Abuse me, if you dare!!<br /> <br /> There are villains in the throne that need its enforcers. Palpatine got Darth Vader, Queen Bavmorda got General Kael. The Gentry needed an enforcer, a guardsman, a lackey, a general for his armies, and got it in the Dark Knight, an inspiration for his troops, and a terror for his enemies, be it other gentry or his own vassals.<br /> <br /> Isabella, bullied as she was in her childhood and adolescence, always wanted to be strong, and imagined herself taking revenge on her abusers. She got imagination, and loved fantastic stories of heroes slashing villains, but with time she fell in love with tragic heroes falling to the dark side for seek of revenge and lack of comprehension from their kind. She began writting tragic fantastic stories of fallen heroes, and she was good at it. So good, that &quot;something&quot; was attracted to her by her stories, most of all for the passion, hatred and pain behind them.<br /> <br /> And one day se received a proposal in dreams, a hand lending help, a paternal figure she never had, wispering: &quot;Do you want the power to exact revenge on those who mistreated you? Do you want to make them suffer for what they did to you? Do you want those who refused help you see their big mistake?&quot;<br /> <br /> She said &quot;Yes, I want&quot;, and the pact it was done.<br /> <br /> Isabella remembers more things than she would like to remember in her durance. A King, a paternal figure that teached her to be strong, to be merciless... and he gave her presents (a sword, an armor, a loyal horse), and love. He cared for her. She was a daughter for him, and he was the father she never had.<br /> <br /> For him, she leaded armies in bloody battles, killed farmers that only demanded not to starve, suffocated rebelions... She was known as the Dark Knight, not a very original nickname, but one she liked, not for the sound of it, but for the tone it was speaked: with fear.<br /> <br /> In a moment of her durance, she realiced that the tale of the &quot;tragic fallen knight seeking revenge on humanity&quot; was not so romantic at all. Something inside her broke, and she became aware of all the bloodshed and misery she brought in the name of her King... no, in the name of herself, of her anger, hatred and frustation. She realized she was used, and worst, she allowed it.<br /> <br /> So the repentant Dark Knight seeked redemption and leaded a rebellion... and she lost.<br /> <br /> She fled to the Hedge, with her loyal mount, Tintaglia, back to the world she belonged, crying for all she lost, all she allowed and all she became, but swearing to use that power for something good, to redeem herself, if redemption was something possible for her.<br /> <br /> The King didn't forget her daughter's treason. Someday she will see her mistake, and she will return to him, repentant. And then she will die at the hands of her substitute, a new Dark Knight replacing the fallen one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 09-29-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:37:27-07:00","id":978708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=978678#post978678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a idea I was working on for a predessigned character for a one shot of a Changeling game. I ended the character development here, I got inspiration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Isabella<br /> <b>Seeming</b>: Fairest<br /> <b>Kith Idea</b>: The Dark Knight (Female <b>Fairest</b> dual kith <b>Razorhand / Metalflesh</b>). Her razorhand weapon is a sword masked in the form of a sword pendant, and when she invokes her Metalflesh armor, it apears in a suit of dark plate mail.<br /> <b>Concept</b>: former Gentry enforcer, leader of the Dark King's armies<br /> <b>Merits ideas</b>: Fae Mount (Tintaglia), Dual Kith, Potent kith.<br /> <b>Motto</b>: Those who abuse the weak are weak themselves. Abuse me, if you dare!!<br /> <br /> There are villains in the throne that need its enforcers. Palpatine got Darth Vader, Queen Bavmorda got General Kael. The Gentry needed an enforcer, a guardsman, a lackey, a general for his armies, and got it in the Dark Knight, an inspiration for his troops, and a terror for his enemies, be it other gentry or his own vassals.<br /> <br /> Isabella, bullied as she was in her childhood and adolescence, always wanted to be strong, and imagined herself taking revenge on her abusers. She got imagination, and loved fantastic stories of heroes slashing villains, but with time she fell in love with tragic heroes falling to the dark side for seek of revenge and lack of comprehension from their kind. She began writting tragic fantastic stories of fallen heroes, and she was good at it. So good, that &amp;quot;something&amp;quot; was attracted to her by her stories, most of all for the passion, hatred and pain behind them.<br /> <br /> And one day se received a proposal in dreams, a hand lending help, a paternal figure she never had, wispering: &amp;quot;Do you want the power to exact revenge on those who mistreated you? Do you want to make them suffer for what they did to you? Do you want those who refused help you see their big mistake?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> She said &amp;quot;Yes, I want&amp;quot;, and the pact it was done.<br /> <br /> Isabella remembers more things than she would like to remember in her durance. A King, a paternal figure that teached her to be strong, to be merciless... and he gave her presents (a sword, an armor, a loyal horse), and love. He cared for her. She was a daughter for him, and he was the father she never had.<br /> <br /> For him, she leaded armies in bloody battles, killed farmers that only demanded not to starve, suffocated rebelions... She was known as the Dark Knight, not a very original nickname, but one she liked, not for the sound of it, but for the tone it was speaked: with fear.<br /> <br /> In a moment of her durance, she realiced that the tale of the &amp;quot;tragic fallen knight seeking revenge on humanity&amp;quot; was not so romantic at all. Something inside her broke, and she became aware of all the bloodshed and misery she brought in the name of her King... no, in the name of herself, of her anger, hatred and frustation. She realized she was used, and worst, she allowed it.<br /> <br /> So the repentant Dark Knight seeked redemption and leaded a rebellion... and she lost.<br /> <br /> She fled to the Hedge, with her loyal mount, Tintaglia, back to the world she belonged, crying for all she lost, all she allowed and all she became, but swearing to use that power for something good, to redeem herself, if redemption was something possible for her.<br /> <br /> The King didn't forget her daughter's treason. Someday she will see her mistake, and she will return to him, repentant. And then she will die at the hands of her substitute, a new Dark Knight replacing the fallen one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right on, I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:04:54-08:00","id":1001788,"title":"","content":"I had a vague for a character, and I'd like some help with fleshing him out.<br /> <br /> I've been wanting to play an ascetic wandering occultist who used to be a Loyalist in the role of cultist. His Keeper was a hoarder and dealer of mystical knowledge in the style of Hermaeus Mora from the Elder Scrolls. His Durance probably involved the studying, crafting and organization of Tokens in the form of grimoires and such, which would be used by other changelings to tempt people into coming to the Realm. <br /> <br /> His first escape consisted of promising to act as a recruiter of cultists in the mortal world. He would come to regret leading people to Arcadia, but at the same time resent the lack of freedom in pursuing the knowledge and mysteries <i>he</i> desired. I am not sure how he would earn his second Seeming, but I would like it to be Wizened. His Kiths would be Antiquarian + Witchtooth.<br /> <br /> Now aware of how the hunger for power can ruin lives, he foregoes a traditional lifestyle in favor of studying the occult all over the Hedge and the Ironside. Occasionally he visits Freeholds to share his expertise and solve mysteries in exchange for minimal goods and services, as well as leads into more mysteries<br /> <br /> He is a brave scholar, a patient teacher and a gifted explorer. On the other hand, he still hasn't gotten rid of the common flaws of cultists, so he is excessively curious and not above using his powers to solve problems. He is not ashamed of admiting his former status as a Loyalist, and prefers that other changelings be similarly frank with him. Unlike many cultists, he makes it a point to treat the objects of his studies with objectivity and keep sane, so his Clarity would be high. He'd probably join the Lord Sages Of The Unknown Reaches. He'd also make it a point to interact with normal folks often so as to not be consumed by his fascination with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> His Mask would probably be something like Nomad, while his Mien is Scholar.<br /> <br /> What do you all think? Is he too much like a typical cultist? What sort of Contracts and Court would best fit him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:15:05-08:00","id":1001794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1001788#post1001788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a vague for a character, and I'd like some help with fleshing him out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Antiquarian and Witchtooth sound about right for Kiths, with the former as his primary one? Also, I can offer alternatives for Witchtooths in the homebrew kiths doc I started - namely my Spellbinder or WhiteOakDragon's Runeskin. As for his Seeming, Wizened would definitely fit.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Lord Sages, I'm still trying to make a conversion of them for 2E. Csre to weigh in your suggestions for them, if you can?<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the subject of Courts, I can see him being on the Autumn Court if he's a Seasonal. If he'S supposed to be part of the Toronto freehold, though, I'd put him with the Brass Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:29:37-08:00","id":1001804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1001794#post1001794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Antiquarian and Witchtooth sound about right for Kiths, with the former as his primary one? Also, I can offer alternatives for Witchtooths in the homebrew kiths doc I started - namely my Spellbinder or WhiteOakDragon's Runeskin. As for his Seeming, Wizened would definitely fit.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Lord Sages, I'm still trying to make a conversion of them for 2E. Care to weigh in your suggestions for them, if you can?<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the subject of Courts, I can see him being on the Autumn Court if he's a Seasonal. If he'S supposed to be part of the Toronto freehold, though, I'd put him with the Brass Court.</div> </div> </div> </div> Runeskin does sound pretty fitting. So do the Courts of Autumn and Brass. I'll have to think more about this.<br /> <br /> Could you please ask me questions about the character so I can round him out? <br /> <br /> I'll take a look at your thread for the Lord Sages later today.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:40:23-08:00","id":1001810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1001804#post1001804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Runeskin does sound pretty fitting. So do the Courts of Autumn and Brass. I'll have to think more about this.<br /> <br /> Could you please ask me questions about the character so I can round him out? <br /> <br /> I'll take a look at your thread for the Lord Sages later today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> Now for your character, does he spend more time in the Hedge or in the mortal world? And either way, does he maintain a Hollow which he can seclude himself in from time to time? I can even argue that the Hollow could be a Mobile one, provided someone can convert the Merit into a 2E enhancement. And I also got a conversion of Ritual Doorway that could allow him to enter it from any part of the globe.<br /> <br /> For Contracts, I imagine those like Murkblur and Nevertread would be useful for him if he likes to travel without leaving much of a trace. Glimpse of a Distant Mirror would also be a good pick as an observer's tool, and a way to check on his collection if he keeps them a room filled with mirrors.<br /> <br /> To make him more of an occultist, might I suggest giving him dots in Professional Training?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-11-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:01:15-08:00","id":1001823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1001810#post1001810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> Now for your character, does he spend more time in the Hedge or in the mortal world? And either way, does he maintain a Hollow which he can seclude himself in from time to time? I can even argue that the Hollow could be a Mobile one, provided someone can convert the Merit into a 2E enhancement. And I also got a conversion of Ritual Doorway that could allow him to enter it from any part of the globe.<br /> <br /> For Contracts, I imagine those like Murkblur and Nevertread would be useful for him if he likes to travel without leaving much of a trace. Glimpse of a Distant Mirror would also be a good pick as an observer's tool, and a way to check on his collection if he keeps them a room filled with mirrors.<br /> <br /> To make him more of an occultist, might I suggest giving him dots in Professional Training?</div> </div> </div> </div> His Hollow would probably be a rustic one without too much in the form of Ammenities. The Ritual Doorway sounds like something he'd use, though.<br /> <br /> I agree with those Contracts, though I imagine he'd keep his possessions in a Token backpack that is bigger on the inside rather than in his Hollow. <br /> <br /> He'd definitely have dots in Professional Training for Occultist.<br /> <br /> Anything else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:53:25-08:00","id":1001866,"title":"","content":"OK, here is his sheet. I'll think of his backstory and appearance later. What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Quote:</b> \u201cWhat do I want in return for teaching you this? Nothing fancy. Just a place to stay, some food and knowing how you got that Token.\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Reginald Rootscroll<br /> <b>Concept: </b>Ascetic Wandering Occultist<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming: </b>Wizened (formerly Loyalist)<br /> <b>Kith: </b>Runeskin (Secondary Affinity: Elemental)<br /> <b>Mask: </b>Nomad<br /> <b>Mien: </b>Scholar<br /> <b>Court:</b> Brass<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Research) 3, Crafts 2, Computer 0, Medicine 2, Occult (Hedge) 3, Politics 0, Investigation (Mysteries) 3, Science 1<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 0, Firearms (Crossbow) 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Survival (Hunting) 3, Weaponry (Knives) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy 2, Expression (Teaching) 2, Intimidation 0, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Hedge), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult), Eye For The Strange, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Hedge), Investigative Aide (Occult), Patient, Professional Training 4 (Occultist: Occult, Investigation, Survival), Trained Observer 1, Anonymity 2, Contacts (Occultists, Survivalists), Resources 1, Arcadian Metabolism, Faerie Healing, Harvest (Goblin Fruit 3), Mantle (Brass 2), Court Goodwill (Autumn 2), Hollow 6 (Size Matters 1, Shadow Garden 1, Escape Route 1, Easy Access 3), Token (Jaw-Bag: Can hold up to Wyrd x 3 units of Size, with a maximum Size of 3 for each one), Token (Rootscroll: gives 9 Again to Occult and Survival, which combines with Professional Training to give 8 Again)<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Clarity: </b>8<br /> <b>Wyrd: </b>3<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts: </b>Bite Of The Wooden Fang, Cloak Of The Elements (Plants 2), Light-Shy, Nevertread, Pathfinder, Dreamsteps<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Prove to the Freehold I am trustworthy, Join a motley that is also interested in the occult, Succumb to the urge of using my powers and expertise for disproportional gain</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-11-2016, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:02:25-08:00","id":1003652,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any idea of how an Elemental <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002074#post1002074\"><b>Merchant</b></a> would earn their Seeming?<br /> <br /> I'm imagining someone who used to think they were smart and charismatic enough to be successful without teamwork and other crucial skills. She frequently lost jobs due to her inflated ego, excessive ambition and poor decisions, until her frustration led her to seek advice from a Gentry in the disguise of a powerful entrepreneur. He took her to his Arcadian Realm, a sprawling and futuristic city filled with goblin and changeling merchants exchanging goods and services from every corner of the Hedge and other dimensions. To teach her humility, her Keeper made her start from the bottom: she would sell goblin fruit and whatever trinkets she could craft herself or find in the trash.<br /> <br /> Forced to quickly face all the mad rules of fae trade, she made bad deal after bad deal without knowing why, contracting an enormous debt that always kept her freedom just out of reach. However, instead of focusing solely on making it out on her own, she decided to pay attention to the talents and needs of others. By throwing away her necessity to always come out on top with no effort or outside help, she learned how those around her used money and were used by it in return. After what seemed like a decade of adapting to the whims of fae consumers and repeatedly coming up with new businesses from scratch, she managed to pay off her debts and escape.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking her Mien would be Idealist, to represent her belief that you either work as a team or not at all. Her Mien would be Predator, to reflect her need to have what others possess that motivates her deep down. Her Court would be either Ivory or Spring.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-15-2016, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:42:02-08:00","id":1009113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1003652#post1003652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any idea of how an Elemental <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002074#post1002074\"><b>Merchant</b></a> would earn their Seeming?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=re4p2ny51s0\" data-code=\"re4p2ny51s0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/re4p2ny51s0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Does that cover it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:10:35-08:00","id":1026748,"title":"","content":"His name is Joon, and to most he is a very large, very angry Korean man who talks to himself. He guards the places and people who hire him with the utmost of his ability, and even those with permission he rarely lets through unscrutinized. Some think him insane, but he gets the job done and he hardly ever moves from his post until told to.<br /> <br /> They don't know how he looks normally - a gigantic helldog, with heads on his shoulders that argue with him. They don't know how he only escaped Arcadia thanks to a hob he chased out from the entrance he was guarding, ignoring the rules of his post like a true animal. They don't know that he was formed from three people, or at least their bodies, becoming the Gargantuan that he is. They don't know how disturbing the thought is that, perhaps, his name isn't really Joon, but that he is really the amalgamation of three personalities. Even those that hear how his shoulders talk can't tell just how depressed he is at the idea that he never existed, that he is a creation of Arcadia as much as a Fetch is.<br /> <br /> Even those that know most of the above don't know precisely what he'd do to his Fetch when he finds it. Just that he is looking for it, desperately.<br /> <br /> Inspiration: <a href=\"http://na.leagueoflegends.com/sites/default/files/styles/scale_xlarge/public/upload/infn-articlebanner.jpg?itok=_ukO-DCx\" target=\"_blank\">http://na.leagueoflegends.com/sites/...?itok=_ukO-DCx</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:31:49-08:00","id":1035715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1026748#post1026748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His name is Joon, and to most he is a very large, very angry Korean man who talks to himself. He guards the places and people who hire him with the utmost of his ability, and even those with permission he rarely lets through unscrutinized. Some think him insane, but he gets the job done and he hardly ever moves from his post until told to.<br /> <br /> They don't know how he looks normally - a gigantic helldog, with heads on his shoulders that argue with him. They don't know how he only escaped Arcadia thanks to a hob he chased out from the entrance he was guarding, ignoring the rules of his post like a true animal. They don't know that he was formed from three people, or at least their bodies, becoming the Gargantuan that he is. They don't know how disturbing the thought is that, perhaps, his name isn't really Joon, but that he is really the amalgamation of three personalities. Even those that hear how his shoulders talk can't tell just how depressed he is at the idea that he never existed, that he is a creation of Arcadia as much as a Fetch is.<br /> <br /> Even those that know most of the above don't know precisely what he'd do to his Fetch when he finds it. Just that he is looking for it, desperately.<br /> <br /> Inspiration: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://na.leagueoflegends.com/sites/default/files/styles/scale_xlarge/public/upload/infn-articlebanner.jpg?itok=_ukO-DCx&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://na.leagueoflegends.com/sites/...?itok=_ukO-DCx</a></div> </div> </div> </div> That really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:47:43-08:00","id":1035720,"title":"","content":"Casey Lords is the Justicar of Themis Banner for the GTA, a book man in his mask, but dripping shadow from his silvery eyes and finger tips in his Mein, reflecting his Shadowsoul kith and membership in the Silver Court. <br /> <br /> Casey has a dark secret, he has a Cambion daughter from before he was taken by his Keeper. <br /> <br /> He joined the Justicars of Themis to protect his daughter from a couple of shields who were hunting her. <br /> <br /> He joined and distracting them with Intel gained from the Silver Court about a huntsmen using dream poison in the area. <br /> <br /> Still he knew he needed real power to protect so he betrayed the Banner of the time to the huntsmen after her, gained a token of reprieve for doing so and took her place as the Banner. <br /> <br /> He then ruled that fathering/mothering a Cambion was only a fine, and only Cambions who created great harm and violence could be put to death in the GTA. Many we're not happy about his ruling, but the High Justicar of Tokyo backed up his decision, as did the Sultina who ruled the Freehold. <br /> <br /> Casey fears his enemies will uncover the truth of his Cambion daughter who he loves dearly, and his act of betrayal of the previous Banner for the GTA. <br /> <br /> For now Casey redirects the attention of the Justicar of Themis towards Huntsmen and Gentry who poison dreams using his contacts, within the Silver Court, which has pleased the current Queen of the Silver Court. <br /> <br /> He is also building a deep alliance with the local Cambion population who are greatful for his mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T05:26:52-08:00","id":1036027,"title":"","content":"This is an NPC from a St. Augustine game that I am starting shortly.<br /> <br /> <b>Djin Forgemaster</b>, Quartermaster to the Freehold of Flames<br /> <b>Wizened Cyclopean </b>of the Ocean Court (Court of Contentment)<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b><br /> A massive hammer for a hand, bellows for lungs, and a eye that spews molten slag, Djin is more workshop than human. Not that he minds. He moves his stocky body with relative ease around his forge, though his discomfort grows elsewhere.<br /> <br /> His mask is a stocky youth, visible uncomfortable with his surroundings. He tends to keep his eyes on the ground, and draws little attention to himself.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> Before his durance Djin was an intelligent youth, more prone to experimentation and projects than applying himself in school. They simply did not teach what he wanted to learn. <br /> <br /> He found his durance to be quite similar. He was forced to build deadly traps and devices, and punished whenever he deviated from his assigned task. But what remained of his body mattered little to him, so long as he could secretly pursue his own work.<br /> <br /> Arcadia bored him, much as his previous life had. One day he viewed his reflection in a gleaming trap and realized he could never truly create under his keeper. So he constructed a majestic trap that flung him free of his bonds and aided in his escape to the hedge.<br /> <br /> <b>Personality:</b><br /> Odd, obsessed, quirky, weird, deadly. All adjectives used to describe Djin even by members of his court. He seems incapable of having a conversation that does not revolve around his craft, and even then rarely makes eye contact, instead looking into his own mind for fresh ideas and inspiration.<br /> <br /> Since his duel with Heartless, the one changeling he could have perhaps called a friend, he has grown increasingly reserved and paranoid. He never creates a weapon that he cannot destroy, he guards his words and plans. And he nurses the injuries bestowed upon him by his fellow freeholder.<br /> <br /> If you are interested in other npcs for this campaign, or in the setting, feel free to ask. The Freehold of Flames is home to Courts of Contentment, Pride, Nostalgia, and Anticipation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:59:54-08:00","id":1036043,"title":"","content":"Does he have a name he uses in public? cause he has to have some human Touchstones right?<br /> <br /> Also, how can I get in on that game if possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:41:29-08:00","id":1036060,"title":"","content":"His touchstones are a bit odd; he tends to only interact with the mortal world in an online medium. He is in no way, shape, or form a people person, and there is very little left of his old life, none of which phases him.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, my game is full, though I plan on posting details about it on the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:39:00-08:00","id":1036225,"title":"","content":"aw shucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:21:34-08:00","id":1036644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thatxygirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1036060#post1036060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His touchstones are a bit odd; he tends to only interact with the mortal world in an online medium. He is in no way, shape, or form a people person, and there is very little left of his old life, none of which phases him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That cannot be good for his Clarity. He also must spend a ton on Goblin Fruits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:53:28-08:00","id":1036665,"title":"","content":"It is certainly bad for his Clarity, but what specific Goblin Fruits are you referencing in your question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T09:23:38-08:00","id":1036675,"title":"","content":"just some basic ones that provide Glamour. If he doesn't go out much, I can't imagine he would have much opportunity to Harvest from emotions. Even if he could get them over the internet, I'd imagine contentment would be a hard emotion to find on Internet Forums","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:33:04-08:00","id":1036701,"title":"","content":"He could still harvest dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:51:19-08:00","id":1036748,"title":"","content":"that's true. I don't know the rules on that, so I don't know if he could just dream-travel to get the stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:52:08-08:00","id":1036750,"title":"","content":"i'm not saying goblin fruit is not a viable option. I know a bunch of characters that do it like that<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:00:56-08:00","id":1036781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1036748#post1036748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's true. I don't know the rules on that, so I don't know if he could just dream-travel to get the stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dream Traveling is a viable option for him. He's definitely patient and methodical enough to work through the process, and doesn't mind spending time in the Hedge. However, he is renowned craftsman of rather intricate weapons, and has been known to work with meteoric iron (cold iron) should the customer provide.So buying from the Goblin Market on the Freehold's doorstep is also a viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","user":"thatxygirl","date":". 01-23-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:24:15-08:00","id":1036791,"title":"","content":"And now, because we can never get enough of THOSE characters:<br /> <br /> <b>Marilyn Heartless</b>, The Whore<br /> <b>Ogre Dearheart/Leechfinger</b> of the Nostalgia Court<br /> <b>Mask/Mien</b>: Addict/Manipulator<br /> <br /> <u><b>Description</b></u><br /> There is not much to see of Marilyn beneath the layers of kudzu and bark that cloak her vaguely feminine form. Her right hand is badly crippled, which she compensates with numerous whipping vines that flawlessly execute her every whim. Some say they have seen deep blue eyes beneath the layers of deadly weeds. They are the unlucky ones.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> Fertility and children seldom come easy to the Lost, and when achieved, it comes at great cost. Marilyn is the youngest of a bloodline cursed by the wants of her elders, though she doubts she shall be the last. The Fertility of this Changeling bloodline expects innocence as payment, and its daughters are inevitably kidnapped on the eve of their 14th year. Some escape, others have their bloodline carried on by their fetches, who have also gained the boon of this great curse.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Personality</u></b><br /> Marilyn Heartless hides behind every distraction she can lay her hands on, whether drugs, changelings or mortals. She is known in the Freehold as the foremost authority of the &quot;Tweeker Hollow,&quot; a hotbed of illicit magical substances and information. She additionally uses her abilities to seek employment at the various vice shops of the local Goblin Market, and the occasional mortal equivalent. And for all her outward signs of struggle and anguish, few Freeholders can match her knowledge of the emotional strengths and weaknesses of her fellow changelings.<br /> <br /> Can elaborate more on this later if need be, gotta run.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","