 in the Freehold as the foremost authority of the &amp;quot;Tweeker Hollow,&amp;quot; a hotbed of illicit magical substances and information. She additionally uses her abilities to seek employment at the various vice shops of the local Goblin Market, and the occasional mortal equivalent. And for all her outward signs of struggle and anguish, few Freeholders can match her knowledge of the emotional strengths and weaknesses of her fellow changelings.<br /> <br /> Can elaborate more on this later if need be, gotta run.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Seems, cool but I'm going to have to look up Kudzu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:17:59-08:00","id":1036827,"title":"","content":"&quot;Kudzu is a group of plants in the genus Pueraria, in the pea family Fabaceae, subfamily Faboideae. They are climbing, coiling, and trailing perennial vines native to much of eastern Asia, Southeast Asia, and some Pacific islands. Wikipedia&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:42:41-08:00","id":1036850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1036827#post1036827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Kudzu is a group of plants in the genus Pueraria, in the pea family Fabaceae, subfamily Faboideae. They are climbing, coiling, and trailing perennial vines native to much of eastern Asia, Southeast Asia, and some Pacific islands. Wikipedia&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> And they are invasive bastards that'll kill any plant gunning for its sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:04:48-07:00","id":1065880,"title":"","content":"I don't have changeling myself but what if I shared one I made using dread powers from HtV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:52:17-07:00","id":1065953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1065880#post1065880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have changeling myself but what if I shared one I made using dread powers from HtV?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested to see how it came out, but maybe post it in Hunter forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:30:57-07:00","id":1066297,"title":"","content":"<b>Spartacus:</b> that is not his name, but it is what the Freehold has taken to calling the Bloodbrute who lead an entire motley of Changelings to freedom from the depths of Arcadia. Since then, they have rallied around him as though he were their messiah. They trust him, they believe in him and they look to him for leadership in a time of chaotic emotion and uncertain futures. Enraged by the torments he suffered at the hands of the Gentry, this Spartacus is not content with merely liberating himself, but plans to free as many slaves as he is capable of during his life time. Among all within the Freehold, he is the one most willing to conduct forays back into Arcadia, undertaking rescue missions to free more Changelings and add to the Freehold's manpower and resources. Occasionally, he frees a slave who feels as strongly as he does about their mistreatment, and they join his motley to help liberate others!<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Bloodbrute<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Fairest<br /> <br /> <b>Mien:</b> A Roman gladiator dressed in light armor forged of bronze and leather. His eyes carry the thousand yard stare of somebody who's seen more combat in a year than most people see in their life time. His hair is dark and wavy and his flesh carries the scars of slavery, including his master's signature brand.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask:</b> A scruffy and rugged man of European descent who's ragged army fatigues and tendency to move around a lot suggest he is a homeless war veteran. His war wounds look worse than they actually are, which earns him no small amount of sympathy and respect from others who honor him for his sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T20:02:23-07:00","id":1072327,"title":"","content":"<b>Jamie Walker:</b> If someone from their freehold was asked by someone to describe the essence of an Elemental, they'd probably just point the questioner at Ol' Jamie. The person who would become the Walker was taken by a Keeper named The Endless, Punishing Wastes for the &quot;crime&quot; of self-centeredness. Dropped alone into an ever-shifting wasteland of the worst that the elements could throw at you, he spent centuries walking endlessly, trying to keep one step ahead of the ever-changing storm that forced him to move on. It was over that time that he was able to reflect on the interconnectedness of all parts of the world and learn his lesson in ways the Wastes never imagined. Forging deals with the very elements that tormented him, he gave up weak flesh and let go of ego, focusing only on his desire to see his family once again and apologize. It was then that they became Jamie Walker. It was a shock to realize how little was left of their communion when they finally returned Ironside. But having survived the worst, there is nothing that can faze them now.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Farwalker/Earthbones<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Elemental<br /> <br /> <b> Mien:</b> You'd have to look closely to really pick out anything human beyond basic shape with them. Their body is a solid mass of stone, with water constantly streaming out of their eye sockets. Paradoxically, they are also always surrounded by a (usually) illusory aura of flames and, also paradoxically, very real cold winds.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask: </b>Gorgeous and intimidating would probably be the first words used to describe them. They look powerfully built; tall, durable and stocky, while still managing the delicate balancing act of androgyny that fits their gender identity. Each of the elements in their Mien is hinted at in their face. Their eyes are a deep blue that draws you in if you look too long. Their skin is as dark as fresh, loamy soil. Their wild hair that seems to move a little constantly is a bright flame-red that most assume is dyed. Oh, and their skin seems to have poor circulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T05:16:51-07:00","id":1101935,"title":"","content":"<b>Pitdog:</b> A text book example of a 90's action hero, Pitdog cares more for actions than words. When he does speak, it is often done so in the form of cool one liners and angry criticism. He serves the Summer Court as their attack dog; they give him a target and he goes to work. Anybody who stands in the way of getting from point A to point B is going to have a bad day, while anybody who stands at the end of point B isn't going to have too many days left to worry about.<br /> <br /> His Keeper used him as a guided weapon, shackled him with magic chains and caged him up until he had need of him. At which point, his Ifrit slave was set loose to destroy his Keeper's foes, only to be dragged back to his cage once more to wait for his next assignment. But over time, his rage grew and the chains began to grow weak from the attempts to contain Pitdog's bestial ferocity. The last time he was let out of his cage, the chains snapped and the Ifrit ran wild, destroying part of his Keeper's own property before digging his way under the security fence and back to freedom!<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> Ifrit<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming:</b> Beast<br /> <br /> <b>Mien:</b> An anthropomorphic dog with features similar to that of a doberman. The black parts of his fur are the color of ebony while the brown parts (as well as his eyes) are the vibrant red of searing hot metal. When he opens his mouth, one can see that his body glows orange with internal flames, with specks of embers being carried upon his breath. His neck is fastened with a thick metal collar from which dangles a broken, three link chain. Truly, he fits the image of a hound escaped from the pits of hell!<br /> <br /> <b>Mask:</b> An ex-military operative who is prone to leaving his upper body exposed whenever possible; allegedly because <i>&quot;it's too hot in here&quot;</i> for him. If he's not going topless, he's wearing sleeveless muscle shirts. The cargo pants and combat boots speak of a man who's either ready for a fight, or just trying to look tough in front of others. His skin is deep tanned from constant exposure to the sun and his eyes are bright green. His body is in good physical condition with strong muscle tone indicating regular strength training. His black hair is shaved into a buzz cut and his default expressions are ones of disgruntlement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-23-2017, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T00:27:28-08:00","id":1174227,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, new to the forums but here's my first attempt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> This is a 1st edition Changeling I hope to convert to 2nd edition once it comes out. <br /> <br /> Name: ...I don't actually have one yet, if anyone wants to make suggestions they'd be appreciated <br /> Concept: Seperated lover and relinquished soldier<br /> Seeming: Wizened <br /> Kith: Soldier <br /> Court: Spring <br /> Contracts: Vainglory \u2022\u2022\u2022, Fleeting Spring \u2022\u2022 <br /> Merits: Fighting Finesse \u2022\u2022, Defensive Combat (Weaponry) \u2022, Quick Draw \u2022, Striking Looks \u2022\u2022, Court Goodwill: Spring \u2022\u2022, Danger Sense \u2022\u2022 <br /> <br /> Mask/ General Discription: Long blonde hair tied into a short pony tail, piecing blue eyes, dresses like a napoleonic style dandy. Stands with a &quot;strength&quot; and keeps his right hand near his waist (where his sword hilt would be). Has a &quot;killer&quot; smile.<br /> <br /> Mein: A more exaggerated form of his mask with pointy ears and radiant skin (could be described as elven using Tolkien's description). A warm breeze and alluring aroma follows him. A higher Wyrd would cause rose petals to shake free from his clothing occasionally before being swept away on a breeze. <br /> <br /> Background: The Swordsmen was once a young lover, whose sense of duty and adventure called him off to serve in the Vietnam War. However, as his platoon was ambushed by enemy forces an explosion knocked him to the ground. Concussed and confused, he accepted the hand offered to help him up. Unbeknown to him, this was the gloved hand of the Noble General. The Noble General dragged The Swordsmen off to Arcadia, who served as his champion in the fey courts. With each victory he was showered in possessions and glamour. However, the time eventually came where he lost a fight, and his keeper, as punishment, took his memories of the one he cared for most. After more fights The Swordsmen came up against a fellow Changeling whom almost rivalled his skill. Upon her defeat she reminded him of the one his keeper had stolen from him. Together, they fought free and escaped into the hedge. Upon escape, the two stuck together for support. The Swordsmen joined the Spring Court, relinquishing his role as a soldier, and hoped to one day fully regain the fragmented memories of his lost love, and find out what became of her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T06:44:03-08:00","id":1174263,"title":"","content":"I like it. It just seems that he sounds more like a Fairest. When I think Tolkien elf, I think Fairest, he has the Fairest's signature Contract and court champion is a standard Fairest role in Arcadia. I think under 2e rules as of now he could easily become a Fairest, but if you want to keep him as Wizened, I'd make him a little less radiant and more of a lean, mean master of combat, changing his description and perhaps his contracts.<br /> <br /> Also, did you mean to put Mantle: Spring \u2022\u2022 instead of Court Goodwill?<br /> <br /> EDIT: How about naming him after a famous swordsman? I'd suggest one of the Three Musketeers or D'Artagnan, except musketeers were supposed to be equally good with rapier and musket (as shown by their name) and he seems to be sword-focused.<br /> <br /> Also, have you considered investing in a Token or Hedgespun blade for him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-08-2018, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T07:24:02-08:00","id":1174270,"title":"","content":"Thanks Aquatosic, <br /> <br /> Ah yes. I have debated with a couple people in regards to if this character should be a fairest or wizened. This may change in 2nd edition, but in 1st ed I ended up mechanically wanting the &quot;Blade Lore&quot; kith blessing from soldier. I then reasoned that while he was treated much like a fairest, he fit more into the category of wizened due to him losing apart of himself (his memories) and becoming &quot;smaller/ less&quot; in a way. He also had basic knowledge of blacksmithing. From what I've read soldiers don't have blade lore in 2nd ed so I'll probably just have to take a proficiency and stop abusing the system, which means I could change him to fairest. <br /> <br /> As to how he got his contracts, they were acquired shortly after leaving the hedge. As his experience in fae courts allowed him to adopt vainglory with some help from his companion. Fleeting Spring came when he officially pledged alligence to them. <br /> <br /> I think I meant court goodwill...his mantle was going to be something I'd put points into at higher wyrd levels. Court Goodwill was allowed for the campaign I played him in as a max of 2 dots at character creation, so I took that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> As a name I did consider D'Artagnan as I am a big fan of the three musketeers...however it did seem clique. <br /> <br /> I didn't post his stats but he had a dot in crafting- blacksmithing (a Swordsmen should be able to look after his sword) and would later further this, looking to make a cold iron blade that could be concealed in his garments while in court. So maybe that would be a token? He was a fresh character and due to him giving up soldiering this wouldn't be important until much later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T08:28:26-08:00","id":1174284,"title":"","content":"So your group was one of the few who didn't houserule any the kith/seeming restrictions? Interesting. How did that go?<br /> <br /> In the end, it's your character, but I'm pretty sure you get a free dot of Mantle at character creation for joining a court anyway, so why not build on that? Court Goodwill is supposed to represent connections with courts outside your own, allowing you to take some of their lesser Contracts. Why handicap yourself by not taking the better option and having another dot to spend on some non-fighting merit to represent how he's trying to grow out of that role?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T17:45:45-08:00","id":1174410,"title":"","content":"Honestly it never occurred to us that your seeming didn't determine your kith. We looked at it as your seeming was what your keeper made you and the kith were flavour and how you escaped. <br /> <br /> This does make sense. I'll have to look over it when second ed roles out and change it \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T18:05:33-08:00","id":1174421,"title":"","content":"Go wild man. The sky's the limit with what you can create with Dual Kith and no kith/seeming restrictions. <br /> <br /> For instance, the Changeling play journal thread Malibu Dream House has a Fairest Minstrel/Windwing (prized songbird), an Elemental Snowskin/Coyote (former trickster tundra spirit Loyalist) and an Elemental Smith/Metalflesh (chivalrous living suit of armor)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-08-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T19:45:35-08:00","id":1174447,"title":"","content":"Should probably do a public update of Danica as a point of compare and contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T20:32:29-08:00","id":1174452,"title":"","content":"Not to derail the thread too much but I do have a character idea and was curious if you knew what the new kith &quot;helldiver&quot; is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T22:34:18-08:00","id":1174470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleOnline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174452#post1174452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to derail the thread too much but I do have a character idea and was curious if you knew what the new kith &quot;helldiver&quot; is?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a kith from the 2e core book; basically, Helldivers are Changelings who can become invisible and intangible (known as Diving) by spending a glamour, and if they observe a gate to another realm being opened they can open it with a glamour like it was a hedgegate. However, to stop Diving they need to spend another glamour, and unless they run into another Helldiver or a Changeling using a specific contract they can't interact with anyone while Diving. Also, unless they find a way of breaking it, each Helldiver has a silver chain from their back to their Keeper that they can be pulled with. Helldiver chain is, itself, an example token.<br /> <br /> Also, since you're not quite up to date on what Kiths are like now, Kiths now grant two powers; one is the Kith Blessing, which grants an exceptional success on 3 successes for a particular skill in a particular circumstance (Artists get it when using a Crafts specialty; Helldivers get it by using Larceny in the Hedge), and if you make your own Kith then the circumstance should be more specific depending on how often a die pool gets used (Brawl or Firearms, for example, are skills that tend to be used a lot when they come up). The second part is Trickery, which is (usually) an ability that is activated by spending a Glamour and rolling a particular die pool; Trickery has a unique name unto itself, but is officially known as, well, Trickery.<br /> <br /> This change in Kiths has likely been why Dual Kith has kind of vanished from the core book as of now. The game is a <i>lot</i> more friendly for custom content, and given how Kiths have two powers to them, a player can now make a custom Kith that has what they want much easier than if they were using two pre-made Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T23:47:46-08:00","id":1174477,"title":"","content":"So can Helldivers enter the Shadow or Twilight/ the Underworld? Does being invisible and intangible mean nothing from these realms can harm them? With this chain attached to them do they run the risk of their keeper dragging them back at any time? <br /> <br /> If duel kithing has disappeared from the core rulebook, why do so many character concepts take the duel kith merit still...do you gain two blessing/trickeries? <br /> <br /> Anywho, thanks for the informative response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:05:07-08:00","id":1174481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleOnline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174477#post1174477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can Helldivers enter the Shadow or Twilight/ the Underworld? Does being invisible and intangible mean nothing from these realms can harm them? With this chain attached to them do they run the risk of their keeper dragging them back at any time?<br /> <br /> If duel kithing has disappeared from the core rulebook, why do so many character concepts take the duel kith merit still...do you gain two blessing/trickeries?<br /> <br /> Anywho, thanks for the informative response.</div> </div> </div> </div>In their durance, yes, they could be pulled back at any time. Once the chain is broken though, they are as free as any Changeling. And no, Diving does not make them any safer than other beings who can do similar tricks by going into Twilight; they see, are seen and interact with other beings that are ephemeral, and if the realm has effectively no Twilight (such as the Underworld), then they are material as well. They also need to eat and sleep like normal, Diving or not.<br /> <br /> Dual Kith is so prominent here because most of the characters here were from before the Kickstarter materials were revealed, and not everyone has access to them. The kickstarter materials, which have been said as being around 90% (or more) ready, do not have the merit, so if you wanted to take it you'd need to effectively balance a character having two Trickeries and two Kith Blessings yourself. That's why I brought up the idea that the benefit of the current system is that everyone has two qualities, without the need to take two Kiths. If you want your character to be able to do something, discuss with the GM and create what you both agree works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:13:20-08:00","id":1174484,"title":"","content":"Aha, that clears that up. If you have a link to the 2nd edition preview (with all the information on Helldivers) that would be greatly appreciated, otherwise thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:13:37-08:00","id":1174485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleOnline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174477#post1174477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can Helldivers enter the Shadow or Twilight/ the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>With access to a suitable entrance, yes. They have to be Diving to do it, but it otherwise works the same as opening a Hedgeway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does being invisible and intangible mean nothing from these realms can harm them? </div> </div> </div>Hard to say, but probably not, looking at the combination of references to how Dive works in the text of the blessing itself and in the Royal Shield Contract Whispers of Morning. A Helldiver can see and interact with pretty much any invisible and intangible entity or object and is specifically able to choose whether changelings using Whispers of Morning can see him, but being in a realm in which ephemeral beings are normally material subjects them to the same limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With this chain attached to them do they run the risk of their keeper dragging them back at any time? </div> </div> </div>They broke the thread as part of their escape; the pieces of such a cord are one of the sample tokens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T06:37:52-08:00","id":1174540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleOnline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174484#post1174484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha, that clears that up. If you have a link to the 2nd edition preview (with all the information on Helldivers) that would be greatly appreciated, otherwise thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> Helldiver<br /> Occasionally, the True Fae need to get places that even they can't reach. Sometimes they need a spy or a thief in their byzantine intrigues, someone who would go unnoticed and unaffected. When they feel like engaging in espionage, the Others create Helldivers.<br /> <br /> Helldivers are unusual among changelings in that they are not only expected to leave Arcadia, they are encouraged to do so. However, this does not free them from their Keepers. Even in their otherworld forms, members of the Helldiver kith still in their durance have a silver thread attached to their person leading back to their Keepers. All Helldivers know the excruciating pain of being yanked out of another realm unexpectedly to face the wrath of their Keeper. Once the thread is broken, the Helldiver is free. Helldivers break their threads in different ways. Some find a goblin smith willing to destroy it (for a price). Some have them broken by the people they were sent to infiltrate. Some simply go through the agony of breaking it themselves.<br /> <br /> Whether in their durance or freed, Helldivers are never in one place for long. They are always chasing some new rumor of a rare token, exploring alien worlds, or listening in on conversations they really shouldn't. Helldivers are hungry for knowledge. After all, knowledge is power.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast: </i>This changeling has bright, inquisitive eyes and vestigial wings. They move with startling speed and are usually content to listen \u2014 that is, until you get them talking.<br /> <i>Darkling: </i>Even when not Diving, she doesn't seem completely solid. Her eyes are constantly roaming the room, checking for threats. She speaks in a hazy, distracted sort of way, as though not all there.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Helldiver uses Larceny in the Hedge, Arcadia, or another unearthly realm, achieving three success counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Dive: </i>Spend a Glamour point to make a Dexterity + Occult roll. On a success, the Helldiver begins to fade into an incorporeal, invisible form. It takes a number of turns equal to (10 - her current Clarity), to a minimum of one full turn, to completely fade. While fading, the Helldiver cannot take any non-reflexive actions or interact with objects or people, and attacks with a non-magical component pass harmlessly through her. Once she completely fades, she acts like a<br /> dematerialized Hedge ghost (p. XX), unable to physically interact with anything except other immaterial beings and objects, such as Hedge ghosts, other Helldivers, changelings using the Whispers of Morning Contract (p. XX), the unquiet dead, and spirits of all stripes. She can see and interact with all of these, no matter their current state. If she can find a gate to another realm, such as the deathly Underworld or mysterious Shadow, she may slip through with a point of Glamour as though it were a Hedgeway (p. XX). If ephemeral beings are normally material in another realm, she becomes so as well. She can spend as much time as she likes Diving, but she still requires basic necessities, such as food and sleep.<br /> To end this effect, spend another Glamour point and make another Dexterity + Occult roll. If successful, the changeling fades back into the world at the same rate she faded out. Should a Helldiver gain the Comatose Condition (p. XX) while Diving, she immediately vanishes from wherever she is to reappear inside her Bastion, as though she had passed through the Gate of Horn to be physically present in her dreams. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:23:51-08:00","id":1174578,"title":"","content":"I'll put down the concept for a changeling character evolution for a mortal PC of mine. You may critique and advise, since the book isn't out yet (but will be by the time I can apply this). Like virtually anything I do, it's long-ish.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Panome</b> was a knight of King Ambrosius Aurelianis, a man of honor, discipline and conviction in a Britain falling increasingly under the enchantment of Merlin. He was also quite skilled, and shared his prowess with a young lady who insisted (as was rarely the case for her gender) on becoming a knight--a feat she achieved by her own qualities, but not before fanning the flames of her competition and honor into a hatred for her teacher that set her firmly on a dark path.<br /> <br /> Merlin's great enchantment hinged on the mystical Celtic cycles of the seasons and its links to mortal rulers, among other side-effects this brought the Hedge closer to the mortal world, fraying the boundaries and permitting a bit of both worlds to leak between. Ideas of chivalry and medieval technology centuries in advance came in vogue within decades, and the Arcadian courts of the British Isles, already arranged in endlessly competing grand coalitions known as the Seelie and Unseelie, peered across with great interest at the burgeoning Glamour of &quot;adventure.&quot; Panome's adventures left him a marked man by an Unseelie queen, and his student's hatred gave the queen agency to affect revenge. He was drawn into the Hedge, and in their final conflict his student pierced Panome's heart with a blackthorn spear and levied a fell curse on him. Though he escaped and fell out once again, the fae magic would not stop; only the fateful (as was his wont) appearance of Merlin enabled Panome to be sent to the best help and treatment the enchanter new: his contact at the Seelie court.<br /> <br /> Panome is not a name. &quot;Panome&quot;, in the imagined tongue of the Seelie courts, means &quot;(an object of) shaped wood.&quot; The Fae do not &quot;help&quot;--the Fae bargain. And Panome paid many things to avoid his fate, but first among them was his name. The Seelie queen, according to their rules, could not un-do the work of her Unseelie sister--but she could warp it and harness it in a way that pleased her. Instead of a will-less creature of black thorns, pain and violence, she could carve a figure of pleasant lines, rich wood and proper bearing. Instead of placing it among the faceless ranks of thorn-maiden garden-guards and goblin-goads, she could put it in her court of fair maidens and brave knights, of endless feasts and thrilling adventures. All beautiful and appropriate to the tales--and affected by nimble &quot;dwarven&quot; craftsmen and their golden tools, without anesthesia, nine times until the &quot;right&quot; result was found.<br /> <br /> Even a master can sometimes struggle to draw out the best from their piece of wood.<br /> <br /> Panome was placed as a fair maiden amidst the fantastic Seelie court. She waited on faerie nobles, danced, cooed at brave knights and listened to their wondrous stories. There was dressing, undressing and the making of dainty clothing. Sometimes she was placed in the forest--for that is where adventure is found, and she was, after all, wood--and there came upon the knight as a Fair Unknown. Often, there was rescuing involved. Occasionally she might be asked for a favor before a joust. Panome was a prop. An extra. And deeply confused by her desire to pick up a sword, strap on some pants and (silver) chainmail and right a wrong in a puissant and honorable fashion. None of the other maids seemed to have this problem--they seemed content to talk incessantly about changing fashion (which always did), who might marry whom (which never did), and who was or was not in favor. There was day and night, but only for the different stages of courtly life, and it was always spring--or maybe early summer, it was hard to tell.<br /> <br /> One day Panome was talking to the dragon--who was really a pretty swell fellow once you get over the fire-breathing (kinda a big deal when you're made of wood)--when she snapped. She remembered--a bit--being a knight. She <i>KNEW</i> how to be a knight. Why should she not be a knight? Go on adventure? Serve his.. er, her.. king? After the knight showed up and killed the dragon (a shame, really, but to be expected), she was carried back to witness his acclaim. In her bag, however, she carried armor, clothes and arms--props from the befated dragon's cave. In the morning, she dressed as a man, set a helm upon her head, and formally requested leave to adventure--the usual custom of hospitality. So granted, she rode her horse out of the Hedge, and back to the world of men.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Fair and shapely, Panome moves with grace and determination, as well as a full measure of recklessness to match the glint in her eyes, making use of a solid firm musculature. Her hair is long and seems to change color in the seasons, from auburn in fall, a brunette-dark in winter, to near-white blond in spring and an almost greenish cast in summer. Especially in spring she's followed by the scent of flowers, and always with an air of the wild. Under the mask she's a woman of polished burl oak wood, so finely and cunningly articulated only a thoughtful finger could find the joins; if you looked very closely, you might see the whorled grain is made from the tiniest of flowing scripts--a language meaningless to most mortals, but writing out the terms and tropes and tales of import to the Fae, and the terms of her own contract with them. Her hair is a mass of living strands, responsive to the seasons, and within the orbits of her face dance eternally a pair of brilliant fireflies.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith:</b> [waiting for the book]<br /> <br /> <b>Seeming: </b>Fairest<br /> <br /> <b>Court and play:</b> Remains to be seen about courts, but the obvious play hooks at work are, that despite escaping Durance she has really changed very little in her circumstances--except now there remains the opportunity to make or reclaim a life, the honor of knighthood that calls her, and fight the curses that are still at work. Her fetch is there, a few years older, muddling along in her place, doing &quot;his&quot; duty but wasting the potential. Can the work of faerie be undone? Can she claim a real name? Sure the land knows lady-knights, but they run right up against stubborn issues of inheritance and legal standing that push women toward traditional power circles and prop-like dynamics....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:39:03-08:00","id":1174584,"title":"","content":"What does her curse manifest as? Also, I think there was a Woodblood kith in 1e? Would that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:12:32-08:00","id":1174594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174584#post1174584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does her curse manifest as? Also, I think there was a Woodblood kith in 1e? Would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keeping in mind that I'm outlining what are <i>very likely</i> but not assured future character situations, the curses would work like this:<br /> <br /> 1. For breaking faerie customs on leaving the Unseelie queen's realm, namely refusing to replace her defeated riverside guardian-knight for all time, a curse that increases recklessness over time. This is independent of the Changeling affliction.<br /> <br /> 2. The Curse of the Black Thorn--struck within the Hedge by a lance of the Unseelie queen's name-wood, transforms the victim into a living thorn-maiden obedient under the queen's orders. This curse will be effectively neutered and amended through the Durance. As you can probably tell, practically speaking the character hasn't gained much in the trade, except the Unseelie Court prefers ugly things, and the Seelie Court pretty things, to human perceptions. The sticking point ultimately that being &quot;pretty&quot; to human perceptions is only an asset if you're not intending already to run contrary to trope!<br /> <br /> 3. The <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiupOvjyMvYAhWBzIMKHYXTBFIQFggpMAA&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FTynged&amp;usg=AOvVaw3mnfuTYjsWBjOSETvGb68j\" target=\"_blank\">Tynged</a> of Math fab Mathonwy - sealed with the pronouncement that he will remain cursed &quot;until [he] knows the full measure of woman's sorrow!&quot; This is heady, Mabinogian stuff, and ensures that unraveling the work of the Fae won't be as easy as, say, picking up every bit of torn soul from the Hedge, or excising what the Seelie queen used as filler and wishing to be a real boy.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I don't know what the Woodblood kith looks like in 1e, but there's a good chance it could work. Mechanical results are less important than collecting the background bits well enough that they can be tied with string and properly animated....<br /> <br /> And yes, the intent is effectively &quot;dryad knight, woo!&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> Edit PS: Having read Woodblood, it's a bit on the plant side and less on the &quot;made of/affinity for wood&quot; side. If 2e wasn't the thing, I'd probably dual-kith it with Woodblood and something else. Since I don't have a playtest document its just feeling around. Maybe something custom... &quot;Xyllic&quot; or whatnot with elements of elemental Fairest at work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T18:32:28-08:00","id":1174728,"title":"","content":"Just looking over some of the 2nd edition Kiths perhaps any of the following would work: <br /> <br /> -Woodblood <br /> -Woodwalker <br /> - Flowering <br /> -Manikin <br /> -Farwalker <br /> <br /> I'm also curious why you picked fairest rather then elemental <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Talking of elementals I should get around to writing my levenquick \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:35:41-08:00","id":1174831,"title":"","content":"I'm not Khanwulf, but I'd say a fair maiden who becomes a knight is a great Fairest concept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:45:11-08:00","id":1174835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OracleOnline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841320-2e-changeling-characters?p=1174728#post1174728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just looking over some of the 2nd edition Kiths perhaps any of the following would work:<br /> <br /> -Woodblood<br /> -Woodwalker<br /> - Flowering<br /> -Manikin<br /> -Farwalker<br /> <br /> I'm also curious why you picked fairest rather then elemental <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Talking of elementals I should get around to writing my levenquick \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23693\" data-vbnamecard=\"23693\">OracleOnline</a>\u200b, I'll file that away for when the plotline gels.<br /> <br /> I've suggested Fairest because the means of escape fits that better than elemental, as well as resonating with the chosen role of the character within the Fae's court. She was an object, a prop, a dressing--but not a natural element itself such as a ... shrubbery. The wood motif is a side-effect of the British Fae courts' (&quot;seelie AND unseelie&quot;) association with the (wild) forest, living cycles, and the like; were it changed to something like alabaster, bronze, samite cloth, down or whatnot the NPC dressing shifts but the core character elements and escape-but-not-really-escape theme remains the same.<br /> <br /> Oh and the PC prefers Fairest, it will make re-linking with mortal plotlines both easier and more conflicting.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T23:08:11-08:00","id":1176897,"title":"","content":"Hi again everyone, <br /> <br /> I'm in the process of creating an elemental. As a levenquick (electric elemental) he was taken because of his dancing/ acrobatic skill, so he could forever create a display as a force of nature. For his durance I pictured him mindlessly becoming lightning to &quot;dance&quot; across a stormy sky. Is there any contracts I can take to represent this? Perhaps skill specialities or merits as well? I was looking at something like the 2nd ed Windwing ability (limited flight), <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T00:27:25-08:00","id":1176908,"title":"","content":"Summon the Loyal Servant could allow you to create electric spritelings, and there is a Sword contract that allows you to make weapons out of an element. Autumn also has a Common contract that lets you create a stormcloud and set lightning bolts down onto others. I need to look into the contracts more to see what else there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T13:22:17-08:00","id":1177031,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <br /> <br /> I should've mentioned until 2nd edition comes out my GM won't let me use second edition rules \ud83d\ude12 <br /> <br /> Currently I'm thinking duel kith with a windwing for flight/glide, for combat my character will resort to elemental armor and primal foundation (combat in a Changeling game hehe). To replicate being able to create objects from his element (electricity, incase anyone's forgotten \ud83d\ude01) I took craft with a specialty in elemental. Examples for this could be to create dancing figures in the palm of his hand, or a staff made of lightning (like the 2nd ed Sword contract). <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23693-oracleonline","name":"OracleOnline","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T17:04:42-08:00","id":1177088,"title":"","content":"Well, Dual Kith isn't really a thing because you're basically able to custom make your own kiths anyways, but how would he use Crafts to create something non-physical? If anything that sounds like Occult with some kind of summon magic. Wouldn't Summon The Loyal Servant do that job, since you can decide the shape and size of your servant when summoning it?<br /> <br /> Edit: right, not second edition. Sorry, only really familiar with that. Point stands on the summon magic though. Crafts are more for making something accurately, whereas making something out of electricity and such...not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}